1
00:02:59,646 --> 00:03:04,646
[chantings]

2
00:03:15,312 --> 00:03:17,812
Padma, wake up and get the kids
ready for school.

3
00:03:19,124 --> 00:03:20,979
The landlord asked for two months' rent.

4
00:03:21,126 --> 00:03:22,687
Oh, God!

5
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,828
Even Lord Venkateshwara is awake.

6
00:03:27,908 --> 00:03:29,211
Mr. Edukondalu hasn't woken up yet.

7
00:03:29,291 --> 00:03:30,578
Wake up.

8
00:03:31,311 --> 00:03:33,412
He doesn't even love his own father.
What a sadist.

9
00:03:37,468 --> 00:03:38,912
Wake up, lazy brother-in-law.

10
00:03:39,291 --> 00:03:40,912
Your sister is even lazier than me.

11
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,035
What is this, Lord Govinda?

12
00:03:51,358 --> 00:03:52,828
Why am I burdened with
these financial troubles?

13
00:03:53,391 --> 00:03:56,645
My age is increasing,
but my SBI bank balance isn't.

14
00:03:57,275 --> 00:04:00,953
I don't see any chance of becoming
a millionaire anytime soon.

15
00:04:01,258 --> 00:04:03,710
Every day, I offer you a handful of roses,

16
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,608
two bananas,

17
00:04:06,013 --> 00:04:08,158
four incense sticks,

18
00:04:08,661 --> 00:04:09,623
three rupees' worth of turmeric,

19
00:04:09,785 --> 00:04:10,790
eight rupees' worth of saffron,

20
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,707
and a fifty-rupee coconut.

21
00:04:12,897 --> 00:04:15,703
I am spending Rs. 100
every day on your offerings.

22
00:04:16,273 --> 00:04:19,287
If you break the coconut quickly,
I'll make chutney out of it.

23
00:04:20,328 --> 00:04:20,828
Shut up!

24
00:04:21,037 --> 00:04:21,703
If God listens to you,

25
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:23,078
he'll misunderstand and think...

26
00:04:23,254 --> 00:04:25,245
...I offer coconuts
for chutney and bananas for juice.

27
00:04:27,259 --> 00:04:31,605
Lord Govinda, every month I have EMIs,
credit card bills, electricity bills,

28
00:04:31,685 --> 00:04:35,751
school fees, hospital expenses, household
expenses, loans, and interest payments.

29
00:04:35,939 --> 00:04:36,426
[Sighs]

30
00:04:36,756 --> 00:04:38,828
There are hundreds of
middle-class problems like these.

31
00:04:41,219 --> 00:04:42,120
One crore rupees...

32
00:04:42,644 --> 00:04:46,873
you just send it through Google Pay or
PhonePe, our lives will be settled, right?

33
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:48,630
-When will you pay the milk bill, sir?
-Oh no!

34
00:04:48,937 --> 00:04:50,340
Are you asking me for the milk bill?

35
00:04:50,894 --> 00:04:51,870
Is this fair, God?

36
00:04:52,477 --> 00:04:54,891
It wasn't the Lord who asked.
It was the milkman.

37
00:04:56,151 --> 00:04:58,203
Venkat, I'll pay it in four days.

38
00:04:58,589 --> 00:04:59,617
Adjust a little.

39
00:04:59,827 --> 00:05:01,349
I'll adjust for your sake, madam.

40
00:05:01,582 --> 00:05:03,745
Hey, if I'm the one paying
the milk bill every month,

41
00:05:03,907 --> 00:05:05,998
how can you adjust for her sake,
you adulterated-milk milkman?

42
00:05:06,157 --> 00:05:07,365
Is that so? Okay, then.

43
00:05:07,552 --> 00:05:08,578
No more adulterated milk from now on.

44
00:05:08,995 --> 00:05:09,995
-See you, madam.
-Ah!

45
00:05:10,507 --> 00:05:11,203
Is that enough?

46
00:05:11,787 --> 00:05:13,447
No more milk for the kids from now on.

47
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,798
I offer you a milk bath every day, right?

48
00:05:18,158 --> 00:05:20,528
But you've left my house without any milk.

49
00:05:20,993 --> 00:05:22,028
What is this, Lord Govinda?

50
00:05:26,694 --> 00:05:27,526
Everything is empty.

51
00:05:27,946 --> 00:05:28,998
This is not a kitchen.

52
00:05:29,184 --> 00:05:30,745
-It has become a scrap metal shop..
-Hi, Bujjulu.

53
00:05:32,746 --> 00:05:33,564
Okay, make coffee.

54
00:05:35,222 --> 00:05:36,946
How can I make coffee without coffee
powder?

55
00:05:37,352 --> 00:05:38,037
You innocent Paddu.

56
00:05:38,229 --> 00:05:39,620
Didn't I bathe without soap in the
morning?

57
00:05:39,870 --> 00:05:41,499
Like that,
you can make coffee without coffee powder.

58
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:42,909
Now you see, dear.

59
00:05:46,119 --> 00:05:46,885
[Groans]

60
00:05:47,078 --> 00:05:48,932
Ouch!

61
00:05:54,009 --> 00:05:54,537
Black coffee.

62
00:05:57,189 --> 00:05:58,906
At the coffee shop, it's Rs. 350.

63
00:06:00,203 --> 00:06:00,912
Dad!

64
00:06:02,162 --> 00:06:02,745
Black coffee.

65
00:06:03,301 --> 00:06:04,847
Brother-in-law, the bank officer called.

66
00:06:05,037 --> 00:06:07,040
If we don't pay the EMI this month,
they'll take the vehicle.

67
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:07,953
Let them take it.

68
00:06:08,469 --> 00:06:11,724
Even if the Finance Minister comes to
help us, we still won't escape poverty.

69
00:06:12,384 --> 00:06:13,582
-Hey, Venkata Ramana.
-What, dad?

70
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:15,474
I've been having a headache since morning.

71
00:06:15,912 --> 00:06:17,453
I suspect it's a brain tumour.

72
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:19,240
Shall we go to Apollo
Hospital for a checkup?

73
00:06:19,637 --> 00:06:23,493
Dad, the bill you pay every month is more
than our rent.

74
00:06:24,258 --> 00:06:25,412
Every headache is a brain tumour to you,

75
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,748
and every gas problem is a heart issue.

76
00:06:26,828 --> 00:06:28,078
I'll end up dying because
of the stress you give me.

77
00:06:28,496 --> 00:06:30,078
Oh, God! What are you saying?

78
00:06:30,356 --> 00:06:31,653
You don't even have insurance.

79
00:06:31,863 --> 00:06:34,879
Oh ho! If I had insurance,
you could've killed me.

80
00:06:36,327 --> 00:06:36,995
Idiot.

81
00:06:37,871 --> 00:06:40,953
[Narrator] 'This middle class Venkata Ramana
has an amazing flashback.'

82
00:06:41,163 --> 00:06:45,859
'Two years ago, he had a hotel called
Venkateswara Tiffin Center.'

83
00:06:46,039 --> 00:06:48,243
'The hotel was packed with people.'

84
00:06:48,566 --> 00:06:50,537
'The cash box was loaded with money.'

85
00:06:50,765 --> 00:06:53,527
'Driven by his urgent desire
to become a millionaire,'

86
00:06:53,607 --> 00:06:57,165
'our hero borrowed Rs.
1 crore at 4% interest...'

87
00:06:57,245 --> 00:06:58,971
'and started grand Venkateswara hotel.'

88
00:06:59,537 --> 00:07:00,787
'It was a huge loss.'

89
00:07:00,995 --> 00:07:02,912
'Due to the huge loss, he became restless.'

90
00:07:03,203 --> 00:07:05,620
'Then he sold the hotel
to Gavvala Govardhan,'

91
00:07:05,828 --> 00:07:07,453
'who worked at the same hotel,
at a huge loss.'

92
00:07:07,841 --> 00:07:12,037
'With that, our people became
workers in their own hotel.'

93
00:07:12,287 --> 00:07:15,003
'Our great Venkata Ramana has
forgotten that he sold the hotel...'

94
00:07:15,162 --> 00:07:17,078
'...and still treats it as his own.'

95
00:07:17,276 --> 00:07:18,100
Venkata Ramana?

96
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,263
Venkata Ramana?

97
00:07:20,162 --> 00:07:21,328
-Oh no!
-Ah!

98
00:07:21,573 --> 00:07:24,551
Sir, I mistook your wife for my wife.

99
00:07:24,715 --> 00:07:26,913
-I was a little confused and thought...
-You will think, man.

100
00:07:27,145 --> 00:07:28,620
You will even think
that the hotel is yours.

101
00:07:28,828 --> 00:07:30,957
Why are you dancing like Prabhu Deva?

102
00:07:31,037 --> 00:07:31,662
It's not that, dear.

103
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:33,328
-Venkata Ramana is...
-Shut up.

104
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:36,529
A dignified housewife should
not talk about other men.

105
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,097
That's fine, Sir.

106
00:07:38,411 --> 00:07:39,287
It's the first day of the month.

107
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,037
Will you pay my salary?

108
00:07:41,337 --> 00:07:42,120
I will pay, man.

109
00:07:42,578 --> 00:07:43,767
Are you begging or what?

110
00:07:44,075 --> 00:07:44,953
First, go and grind the batter.

111
00:07:48,410 --> 00:07:50,577
[Temple bell rings]

112
00:07:52,685 --> 00:07:53,870
What are these struggles, God?

113
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:56,370
Since childhood, I have lived with
a shaved head more than with hair.

114
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:57,912
My grandfather's name is Srinivasulu.

115
00:07:58,332 --> 00:07:59,427
My father's name is Edukondalu.

116
00:07:59,765 --> 00:08:00,837
My name is Venkata Ramana.

117
00:08:01,953 --> 00:08:05,524
Since my wife's name is Padmavathi,
I married her without dowry.

118
00:08:06,559 --> 00:08:07,699
Why am I facing these problems?

119
00:08:11,495 --> 00:08:14,480
God, this is your devotee
Venkata Ramana's plea.

120
00:08:14,662 --> 00:08:16,243
I don't know what you will do.

121
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:19,870
End all my troubles and
make me a millionaire.

122
00:08:20,645 --> 00:08:22,537
Om namo Venkateshaya.

123
00:08:33,495 --> 00:08:34,537
What is this, Venkata Ramana?

124
00:08:35,156 --> 00:08:37,526
Do you think it's an
offering box or a post box?

125
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:39,694
Recently, we opened the offering box.

126
00:08:39,912 --> 00:08:41,453
More than half of it was
filled with your letters.

127
00:08:41,808 --> 00:08:42,970
Everyone is offering money.

128
00:08:43,203 --> 00:08:44,120
But you are offering letters.

129
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:46,703
Everyone has money.
But I have problems.

130
00:08:47,399 --> 00:08:50,453
That's why I wrote all my problems in this
letter and put it in the offering box.

131
00:08:51,843 --> 00:08:53,495
He is looking at it, but not paying
attention.

132
00:08:54,299 --> 00:08:55,790
Lord Edukondala Venkata Ramana.

133
00:08:56,052 --> 00:08:56,994
Consider me, God.

134
00:08:57,074 --> 00:08:58,011
Hail Lord Govinda.

135
00:09:02,709 --> 00:09:03,828
Credit at the grocery store,

136
00:09:04,037 --> 00:09:05,146
credit at the vegetable vendor,

137
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:06,328
credit with the laundry guy,

138
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:07,707
credit with the milkman,

139
00:09:08,399 --> 00:09:09,412
credit with the house owner,

140
00:09:09,578 --> 00:09:10,603
credit for school fees,

141
00:09:10,818 --> 00:09:11,870
and credit at the barber shop.

142
00:09:11,950 --> 00:09:13,203
Credit... Credit... Credit.

143
00:09:14,090 --> 00:09:16,037
I'm getting tired of answering questions,
Karuna.

144
00:09:16,237 --> 00:09:18,332
I switched off the phone, sister-in-law.

145
00:09:18,618 --> 00:09:19,203
Padma.

146
00:09:20,249 --> 00:09:20,912
Padma.

147
00:09:21,468 --> 00:09:22,162
It's you I'm calling.

148
00:09:23,699 --> 00:09:24,662
Why aren't you answering?

149
00:09:24,936 --> 00:09:26,436
Are you at home or in Singapore?

150
00:09:28,564 --> 00:09:30,205
Oh, it's Singapore.

151
00:09:30,552 --> 00:09:31,920
There are only three poors in our house.

152
00:09:32,145 --> 00:09:34,537
Kitchen poor, Bedroom poor, Hall poor.

153
00:09:34,703 --> 00:09:35,933
All are poor.

154
00:09:38,305 --> 00:09:40,077
Why is my darling angry?

155
00:09:41,577 --> 00:09:42,703
Let me cool down.

156
00:09:43,162 --> 00:09:43,912
Darling.

157
00:09:45,412 --> 00:09:46,412
What happened, darling?

158
00:09:46,678 --> 00:09:47,662
Why are you irritated?

159
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:50,870
You are very rich in this aspect.

160
00:09:51,365 --> 00:09:52,662
Padhu, you don't worry.

161
00:09:53,037 --> 00:09:55,537
A Singapore tour for our
next wedding anniversary.

162
00:09:56,128 --> 00:09:57,412
That will not happen in this life.

163
00:09:57,853 --> 00:09:59,390
I know all these things.

164
00:09:59,634 --> 00:10:00,675
He is a negative mind.

165
00:10:01,519 --> 00:10:02,412
Hey, my salary got credited.

166
00:10:03,253 --> 00:10:03,957
All of you come here.

167
00:10:04,037 --> 00:10:04,995
We have to divide the budget.

168
00:10:05,925 --> 00:10:07,870
Padhu, all of you keep
your cell phones here.

169
00:10:10,688 --> 00:10:13,870
Salaries are credited via PhonePe
and debited via Google Pay.

170
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:18,217
Padma, your salary is for house rent.

171
00:10:18,662 --> 00:10:20,485
Karuna, your salary is for household
expenses.

172
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:23,101
Seenu, your salary is for school fees.

173
00:10:24,076 --> 00:10:25,120
My salary goes toward these EMIs.

174
00:10:25,623 --> 00:10:27,870
Brother-in-law, give Rs.3500 to the
chicken shop owner.

175
00:10:27,950 --> 00:10:28,828
Otherwise, he won't be happy.

176
00:10:29,287 --> 00:10:30,787
From today, no chicken or mutton.

177
00:10:31,828 --> 00:10:35,091
Venkata Ramana, get my eyes
checked at Prasad Eye Hospital.

178
00:10:35,569 --> 00:10:36,165
-Father!
-Hmm.

179
00:10:36,245 --> 00:10:39,332
I will offer you my eyes, just as Thippadu
offered his to Lord Shiva in Kannappa.

180
00:10:39,525 --> 00:10:40,332
Close your eyes and sleep.

181
00:10:40,412 --> 00:10:41,453
-Hubby!
-Hmm.

182
00:10:41,832 --> 00:10:45,318
We've managed the household expenses.
How will we pay the interest to Masthan?

183
00:10:46,359 --> 00:10:47,662
Our problems are like
an inexhaustible pot.

184
00:10:47,906 --> 00:10:50,203
One problem is almost solved,
and another one is already there.

185
00:10:51,450 --> 00:10:52,370
Let them come.

186
00:11:04,013 --> 00:11:04,707
Venkata Ramana.

187
00:11:05,016 --> 00:11:06,957
Come to the hall,
or I will come into your kitchen.

188
00:11:07,203 --> 00:11:07,832
Hello, brother.

189
00:11:07,912 --> 00:11:08,495
Bhai... Bhai.

190
00:11:08,822 --> 00:11:10,754
I just arrived. Why are you saying bye?

191
00:11:10,953 --> 00:11:11,745
I didn't say bye, brother.

192
00:11:12,019 --> 00:11:12,790
I said "bhai" (brother).

193
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:14,288
Forget all that respect stuff.

194
00:11:14,457 --> 00:11:16,163
First, Tell me when you will give me Rs.
18 lakhs.

195
00:11:16,585 --> 00:11:17,745
I will give you in a few days.

196
00:11:18,245 --> 00:11:20,370
Taj Mahal is built by Shah Jahan.

197
00:11:20,823 --> 00:11:22,537
Charminar is built by Qutub Shah.

198
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,203
I will build your grave.

199
00:11:24,787 --> 00:11:26,185
Talk with respect.

200
00:11:27,273 --> 00:11:29,786
Though we don't pay the principal,
we are paying interest every month, right?

201
00:11:38,203 --> 00:11:39,120
You are so pretty.

202
00:11:40,098 --> 00:11:41,953
But my wife is not as pretty as you.

203
00:11:42,770 --> 00:11:44,995
You are very lucky, Venkata Ramana.

204
00:11:46,735 --> 00:11:49,745
Even if a man works hard, it is useless.

205
00:11:50,616 --> 00:11:55,173
But if a woman works hard,
she earns full money.

206
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:57,870
-You will get rid of all the loans.
-Hey!

207
00:11:57,950 --> 00:11:59,540
-Hey!
-What are you saying?

208
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:03,328
[crosstalk]

209
00:12:03,535 --> 00:12:04,287
All of you, keep calm.

210
00:12:05,306 --> 00:12:06,790
[Snaps fingers] I will settle it now.

211
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:08,785
From today, I will stay here, sleep here,

212
00:12:08,972 --> 00:12:09,953
-Listen to me.
-bath here,

213
00:12:10,181 --> 00:12:12,123
eat here., drink here, die here...

214
00:12:12,203 --> 00:12:12,870
Stop it.

215
00:12:34,341 --> 00:12:36,203
Husband, come inside once.

216
00:12:52,328 --> 00:12:52,995
Adorn me with it.

217
00:12:53,203 --> 00:12:56,075
Padma, I will convince
Masthan by pleading with him.

218
00:12:56,155 --> 00:12:56,703
Adorn me with it.

219
00:12:57,578 --> 00:12:58,537
Think about it once, Padma.

220
00:12:58,745 --> 00:12:59,453
First, Adorn me with it.

221
00:13:05,787 --> 00:13:08,272
First sell this gold and pay the interest.

222
00:13:08,352 --> 00:13:10,536
-No, Padma. What I am saying is...
-Listen to me. Go.

223
00:13:15,411 --> 00:13:16,453
Come, Venkata Ramana. Sit.

224
00:13:19,310 --> 00:13:20,287
You came to pawn gold again?

225
00:13:21,251 --> 00:13:22,162
No, buy it.

226
00:13:22,573 --> 00:13:24,162
-Brother, weigh this.
-Okay.

227
00:13:27,391 --> 00:13:28,123
It is 10 grams.

228
00:13:28,319 --> 00:13:29,584
You will get Rs. 1,35,000.

229
00:13:30,828 --> 00:13:31,787
Okay, give it to me.

230
00:13:37,131 --> 00:13:38,078
Greetings, priest.

231
00:13:38,745 --> 00:13:39,707
Where are you going?

232
00:13:39,787 --> 00:13:42,325
Venkata Ramana, your face is glowing.

233
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:43,900
There is no glow.

234
00:13:44,370 --> 00:13:46,328
I'm forced to sell my wife's
nupital chain to clear the loans.

235
00:13:46,787 --> 00:13:47,495
Don't worry.

236
00:13:47,912 --> 00:13:50,582
Lord Venkateswara will
take care of everything.

237
00:13:50,662 --> 00:13:51,703
I also believe that.

238
00:13:51,995 --> 00:13:52,995
He don't ...

239
00:13:53,454 --> 00:13:56,578
[Groans]
- Priest... Priest... Priest.

240
00:13:56,828 --> 00:13:58,495
Why are you falling
like the share market?

241
00:13:58,864 --> 00:13:59,960
Auto, Ola, Uber.

242
00:14:03,203 --> 00:14:04,328
Doctor! Doctor!

243
00:14:06,448 --> 00:14:06,995
Yes.

244
00:14:07,578 --> 00:14:12,203
I am Dr. Vishnu Varadhan,
MBBS, FRCS, BHMS, BAMS.

245
00:14:12,953 --> 00:14:14,998
What is this, sir? You read out
all the transport company names.

246
00:14:15,078 --> 00:14:16,370
Those are not the names
of transport companies.

247
00:14:16,953 --> 00:14:18,037
Those are the degrees
awarded to the doctor.

248
00:14:19,368 --> 00:14:20,412
What is his problem?

249
00:14:20,708 --> 00:14:22,209
Oh my God!

250
00:14:22,412 --> 00:14:24,203
All the walls in his body are blocked.

251
00:14:24,412 --> 00:14:25,340
Husband! [Crying]

252
00:14:25,537 --> 00:14:26,745
Sister, don't cry.

253
00:14:27,009 --> 00:14:29,962
If we perform an immortality ritual in
his name, he will recover instantly.

254
00:14:30,693 --> 00:14:32,953
Once your brother-in-law gets up,
take him home,

255
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,893
do the ritual, and give him sacred food.

256
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,078
MBBS doctor here.

257
00:14:37,528 --> 00:14:39,832
-Does he have health insurance?
-No, doctor.

258
00:14:39,912 --> 00:14:40,537
No?

259
00:14:41,078 --> 00:14:42,912
We will proceed with surgery
only if the amount is paid.

260
00:14:45,403 --> 00:14:46,387
Doctor, I will leave.

261
00:14:46,828 --> 00:14:47,703
Take care of him.

262
00:14:50,745 --> 00:14:51,537
Venkate Ramana.

263
00:14:52,735 --> 00:14:53,747
If anything happens to me,

264
00:14:54,965 --> 00:15:00,055
write a letter in my name asking the God
to take care of my wife and children,

265
00:15:01,302 --> 00:15:04,120
and put it in Lord
Venkateswara's offering box.

266
00:15:04,575 --> 00:15:05,245
Will you do it?

267
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,453
Doctor, how much will it cost?

268
00:15:08,728 --> 00:15:09,578
It will be Rs.1,35,000.

269
00:15:11,625 --> 00:15:13,703
How do you know that I have Rs.1,30,000?

270
00:15:14,024 --> 00:15:15,412
Do you have a scanning
machine in your eyes?

271
00:15:16,706 --> 00:15:18,674
You have the Rs.1,35,000 bundle.

272
00:15:18,953 --> 00:15:22,144
If you pay the amount at the counter,
we will perform the surgery.

273
00:15:38,328 --> 00:15:38,953
What is this?

274
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,293
It is biriyani.

275
00:15:40,612 --> 00:15:42,581
This family doesn't know about biryani.

276
00:15:45,637 --> 00:15:47,620
By the way, will you pay via Google Pay,
PhonePe, or cash?

277
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:50,596
Why are you looking at me like that?

278
00:15:51,703 --> 00:15:52,287
Give it to me.

279
00:15:54,019 --> 00:15:55,370
Mastan Bhai, come out for a minute.

280
00:16:00,018 --> 00:16:00,620
Give me the money.

281
00:16:02,245 --> 00:16:04,953
Mastan Bhai, do you know Venkateshwara
Swami's temple priest?

282
00:16:05,162 --> 00:16:05,828
Yes, I know him.

283
00:16:06,102 --> 00:16:07,870
He has a heart problem.

284
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:11,707
So, you took an auto and
took him to the hospital.

285
00:16:11,787 --> 00:16:12,995
And you paid money for his treatment.

286
00:16:13,787 --> 00:16:15,495
How could you say it as if
you saw it in the CCTV camera?

287
00:16:15,703 --> 00:16:19,328
This is the first thing that
every idiot who takes a loan says.

288
00:16:19,995 --> 00:16:20,537
Damn!

289
00:16:22,495 --> 00:16:24,177
Give me the money, man.
Don't make it an issue.

290
00:16:31,828 --> 00:16:33,662
My father's surgery is done, sir.

291
00:16:34,012 --> 00:16:36,453
-They said that he is fine now.
-Oh! Good.

292
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:40,078
My husband has been worshipping God in the
temple for many years.

293
00:16:40,412 --> 00:16:42,920
But we don't know how God looks like.

294
00:16:43,726 --> 00:16:48,816
From today,
whenever I close my eyes and think of God,

295
00:16:49,491 --> 00:16:50,828
I will see you.

296
00:16:51,287 --> 00:16:53,420
Oh no! Why are you touching my feet?

297
00:16:53,662 --> 00:16:54,457
Is he fine?

298
00:16:54,667 --> 00:16:55,870
-Yes, he is fine.
-I'm happy.

299
00:16:56,167 --> 00:16:58,539
[Sobbing]

300
00:17:05,195 --> 00:17:06,495
Hey, Mastan Bhai.

301
00:17:07,162 --> 00:17:08,120
Why are you crying?

302
00:17:08,439 --> 00:17:10,155
My father always used to say one line.

303
00:17:11,411 --> 00:17:14,663
A rich man's help is charity,
but a poor man's help is divine.

304
00:17:15,828 --> 00:17:17,588
A person like you fed
biryani to your neighbours...

305
00:17:18,066 --> 00:17:19,787
...even when there were
no groceries at home.

306
00:17:21,216 --> 00:17:22,631
I am telling you the truth, brother.

307
00:17:22,819 --> 00:17:23,953
There is a God in you.

308
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:26,037
Least but not last.

309
00:17:27,234 --> 00:17:28,703
In these two Telugu states,

310
00:17:29,391 --> 00:17:33,544
your family is the only one eligible
for every government welfare scheme.

311
00:17:34,069 --> 00:17:35,540
Brother, listen to me.

312
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:36,526
Keep this Rs. 10,000.

313
00:17:36,995 --> 00:17:38,644
-Brother, this is...
-Give him what you can.

314
00:17:40,379 --> 00:17:40,953
Keep it up.

315
00:17:53,203 --> 00:17:54,881
Even God cannot save you.

316
00:18:03,535 --> 00:18:06,787
If God wants to save me,
no one can stop him.

317
00:18:13,828 --> 00:18:15,498
I am working on it. Let's do it.

318
00:18:16,078 --> 00:18:16,745
-Ah!
-Greetings, sir.

319
00:18:17,078 --> 00:18:18,133
Hey, Venkat Ramana.

320
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:21,174
If someone searches "fool" on Google,
they'll get your name, right?

321
00:18:21,254 --> 00:18:21,748
Why, sir?

322
00:18:21,828 --> 00:18:22,953
Why do you ask?

323
00:18:23,162 --> 00:18:26,245
You saved a priest's life by selling
your wife's nuptial chain, right?

324
00:18:27,076 --> 00:18:29,453
Is social service necessary
for a poor family?

325
00:18:29,995 --> 00:18:32,328
Go and wear your uniform and do your duty.

326
00:18:32,537 --> 00:18:34,203
[wailing in pain]

327
00:18:34,412 --> 00:18:35,287
-Sister-in-law...
-Karuna...

328
00:18:35,453 --> 00:18:36,423
-Brother...
-Karuna...

329
00:18:36,648 --> 00:18:37,953
-Karuna...
-Karuna...

330
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,328
Let's take her to the hospital.

331
00:18:39,676 --> 00:18:41,203
[wailing in pain]

332
00:18:42,141 --> 00:18:42,828
Doctor...

333
00:18:43,669 --> 00:18:44,953
-Doctor...
-Shh!

334
00:18:46,482 --> 00:18:47,287
This is a hospital.

335
00:18:50,269 --> 00:18:51,245
There is no problem, right?

336
00:18:52,078 --> 00:18:52,703
There is a problem.

337
00:18:53,578 --> 00:18:56,245
If you pay Rs. 50,000,
the problem will be solved.

338
00:18:56,607 --> 00:18:57,912
Otherwise, it is will be a big problem.

339
00:18:58,370 --> 00:18:59,203
Cash and delivery.

340
00:19:00,412 --> 00:19:01,623
If you give us a loan...

341
00:19:01,703 --> 00:19:03,947
The hospital is already
under a Rs. 3 crore loan.

342
00:19:04,622 --> 00:19:06,745
To pay the EMI, my body is trembling...

343
00:19:07,012 --> 00:19:08,370
...my heart, I mean.

344
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:12,328
Doctor, please ensure my wife's delivery
is safe, even if I must sell my kidneys.

345
00:19:12,571 --> 00:19:14,787
This is not a military hotel to sell
kidneys and idlis.

346
00:19:15,149 --> 00:19:15,912
This is a hospital.

347
00:19:16,495 --> 00:19:18,256
Delivery on cash.

348
00:19:18,336 --> 00:19:18,995
Do you understand?

349
00:19:32,258 --> 00:19:32,912
I don't have money.

350
00:19:33,729 --> 00:19:34,703
I don't have anyone to lend me money.

351
00:19:36,078 --> 00:19:37,432
What kind of life is this, Venkata Ramana?

352
00:19:51,468 --> 00:19:56,634
Give me money for the operation
and prove you are a saviour, God.

353
00:19:58,105 --> 00:20:00,037
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

354
00:20:00,337 --> 00:20:04,069
[Sanskrit]

355
00:20:15,056 --> 00:20:17,888
Do something and help me
get the money, God.

356
00:20:21,745 --> 00:20:22,412
Where did you get the money?

357
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:23,870
My friend Mary gave me the money.

358
00:20:24,984 --> 00:20:28,293
[chanting Lord Venkateswara hymns]

359
00:20:29,015 --> 00:20:29,873
He is Lord Vinayaka.

360
00:20:29,953 --> 00:20:30,778
He is not Lord Govinda.

361
00:20:31,171 --> 00:20:32,578
For me, every God is Lord Govinda.

362
00:20:32,912 --> 00:20:33,703
Isn't it, Lord Govinda?

363
00:20:36,453 --> 00:20:38,578
SRI VARALAKSHMI SUPER MARKET

364
00:20:38,849 --> 00:20:40,662
Gulab jamun for the kids.
It has a buy-one-get-one offer.

365
00:20:41,539 --> 00:20:42,953
Tamarind for my cute wife.

366
00:20:43,405 --> 00:20:44,120
Dried chillies.

367
00:20:44,783 --> 00:20:45,578
Zandu Balm for my father's headache.

368
00:20:45,795 --> 00:20:47,839
-Hi, brother.
-Hi Mary.

369
00:20:48,158 --> 00:20:50,393
-How are you?
-I heard your sister got delivered.

370
00:20:50,473 --> 00:20:52,677
Yes. I wanted to name
the baby girl after you.

371
00:20:52,977 --> 00:20:54,327
You are not Mary, you are Mother Mary.

372
00:20:54,561 --> 00:20:56,207
Me? What did I do, brother?

373
00:20:56,389 --> 00:20:57,842
You gave Rs.50,000
when Padma asked you.

374
00:20:58,078 --> 00:20:59,037
Rs.50,000?

375
00:21:00,177 --> 00:21:03,373
I called her 25 times for
my old loan of Rs. 25,000,

376
00:21:03,453 --> 00:21:05,333
and she blocked my number.

377
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,880
Didn't you give her the money?

378
00:21:19,846 --> 00:21:20,877
-Father-in-law.
-Dear.

379
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:21,745
Take your tablets.

380
00:21:21,953 --> 00:21:22,578
Give it to me.

381
00:21:24,571 --> 00:21:25,328
Padma.

382
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:28,412
What is it?

383
00:21:28,995 --> 00:21:29,745
Where did you get the money?

384
00:21:30,702 --> 00:21:32,334
I told you my friend Mary
gave it to me, right?

385
00:21:35,953 --> 00:21:37,332
I am asking you,
where did you get the money?

386
00:21:37,412 --> 00:21:38,245
Are you deaf?

387
00:21:38,412 --> 00:21:39,908
I told you my friend Mary
gave it to me, right?

388
00:21:44,727 --> 00:21:46,037
I will kill you. Tell me the truth.

389
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:47,431
-What is it, brother-in-law?
-No.

390
00:21:47,511 --> 00:21:48,889
-Ramana.
-No one talk in the middle.

391
00:21:53,670 --> 00:21:55,751
What mistake did you do that
you're afraid to tell the truth?

392
00:21:55,967 --> 00:21:57,205
She committed theft.

393
00:22:01,001 --> 00:22:03,148
Thinking there was no
CCTV camera in the hotel,

394
00:22:03,327 --> 00:22:04,770
she opened the cash counter,

395
00:22:05,051 --> 00:22:07,453
took Rs. 50,000, and
hid it under her dress.

396
00:22:10,077 --> 00:22:12,467
Sorry, sir.
We will be careful not to repeat it again.

397
00:22:13,405 --> 00:22:15,065
It's not you to be careful.

398
00:22:15,245 --> 00:22:16,415
I will be careful.

399
00:22:16,687 --> 00:22:18,974
None of you have to
come to work from today.

400
00:22:19,162 --> 00:22:22,706
Sir, if you fire us, we will struggle
to manage food and medicines.

401
00:22:23,078 --> 00:22:27,159
I don't have the heart to
employ this family of thieves.

402
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:33,168
If you don't return the money you
stole from the hotel within a week,

403
00:22:33,870 --> 00:22:38,953
I'll sell this kid to beggars.
After all, I paid for his birth.

404
00:22:40,453 --> 00:22:42,078
I already have a buyer lined up.

405
00:22:45,347 --> 00:22:46,328
Goodbye, Govinda.

406
00:23:07,012 --> 00:23:10,162
I used to chant your name,
'Govinda', every minute.

407
00:23:11,081 --> 00:23:14,912
In return, you made my wife a thief.

408
00:23:18,646 --> 00:23:20,953
This is the final meeting and
the final words between us.

409
00:23:23,315 --> 00:23:24,956
I won't pray to you again.

410
00:23:26,118 --> 00:23:27,215
I will not come to your temple again.

411
00:23:30,955 --> 00:23:39,122
[Sanskrit]

412
00:24:14,498 --> 00:24:18,252
If anyone brings him down,
that will be my last day.

413
00:24:37,661 --> 00:24:42,370
Brother-in-law, no one is getting a job no
matter how hard we try.

414
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:46,245
Brother, this is happening
because you kept God in the attic.

415
00:24:46,453 --> 00:24:48,120
Brother, please bring God down from there.

416
00:24:48,831 --> 00:24:51,842
Venkata Ramana, I don't care if
I don't get medical tests done.

417
00:24:52,203 --> 00:24:53,620
Bring the God down.

418
00:24:54,596 --> 00:24:56,037
He won't listen even if we tell him.

419
00:24:56,828 --> 00:24:57,370
So obstinate.

420
00:25:02,753 --> 00:25:05,413
[Cell phone rings]

421
00:25:06,491 --> 00:25:09,069
-Hello.
-You applied for a security job, right?

422
00:25:09,370 --> 00:25:10,499
Your job is confirmed.

423
00:25:11,647 --> 00:25:12,703
Say it louder once.

424
00:25:13,534 --> 00:25:16,415
-You applied for a security job, right?
-Yeah.

425
00:25:16,495 --> 00:25:18,412
-Your job is confirmed.
-Oh!

426
00:25:18,662 --> 00:25:19,915
Rs. 18,000 salary.

427
00:25:19,995 --> 00:25:21,912
-How much?
-Rs. 18,000 salary.

428
00:25:21,992 --> 00:25:24,268
-Oh!
-Rs. 3,000 PF.

429
00:25:25,078 --> 00:25:27,127
Rs. 25 lakhs Medical insurance.

430
00:25:27,328 --> 00:25:29,494
-How much is the medical insurance?
-Rs. 25 lakhs.

431
00:25:30,572 --> 00:25:31,953
Come to the agency tomorrow morning.

432
00:25:32,620 --> 00:25:33,714
Aha!

433
00:25:35,507 --> 00:25:36,620
I got a job today.

434
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:39,397
In a week, all of you will get a job.

435
00:25:41,745 --> 00:25:44,995
I don't need anyone's
kindness or compassion.

436
00:25:52,429 --> 00:25:53,245
You go to Shamirpet.

437
00:25:53,495 --> 00:25:54,287
You go to Ameerpet.

438
00:25:54,495 --> 00:25:55,347
You go to Kokapet.

439
00:25:55,537 --> 00:25:56,332
You go to Dhulpet.

440
00:25:56,412 --> 00:25:57,738
Which place should I go to, sir?
Is it Amberpet?

441
00:25:58,007 --> 00:26:01,206
You are the night watchman at Srinagar
Colony Lord Venkateshwara temple.

442
00:26:01,827 --> 00:26:03,139
Lord Venkateshwara temple?

443
00:26:03,315 --> 00:26:04,839
[Temple bell rings]

444
00:26:08,037 --> 00:26:09,281
I know it very well.

445
00:26:10,019 --> 00:26:11,273
You are very egoistic.

446
00:26:11,953 --> 00:26:15,163
As I kept you in the attic, did you
keep me at the steps of your temple?

447
00:26:15,878 --> 00:26:16,851
I will teach you a lesson.

448
00:26:17,078 --> 00:26:18,140
Hey, Venkata Ramana.

449
00:26:18,495 --> 00:26:20,328
Why are you angry with God?

450
00:26:21,714 --> 00:26:22,953
No talking between us.

451
00:26:23,249 --> 00:26:25,870
[Laughs] I can see the sulking
Annamayya in you.

452
00:26:27,662 --> 00:26:31,787
On the day of God's marriage ritual,
you became security for the Almighty.

453
00:26:32,245 --> 00:26:33,537
How lucky you are.

454
00:26:33,953 --> 00:26:35,354
He will take care of you.

455
00:27:02,717 --> 00:27:05,447
[Cell phone rings]

456
00:27:08,131 --> 00:27:08,828
Hello, dear.

457
00:27:09,037 --> 00:27:09,912
The kids want to talk to you.

458
00:27:10,662 --> 00:27:12,203
Hey, your father is on the call.

459
00:27:13,412 --> 00:27:15,745
-Hello.
-Should I bring chocolates when I come?

460
00:27:16,037 --> 00:27:17,939
Bring the school fees, daddy.

461
00:27:19,370 --> 00:27:22,591
They told me not to come to school
from tomorrow without the fee.

462
00:27:23,453 --> 00:27:24,037
Wait.

463
00:27:24,620 --> 00:27:25,203
Study.

464
00:27:26,810 --> 00:27:28,412
-Hubby.
-Yes.

465
00:27:28,620 --> 00:27:29,662
Don't worry.

466
00:27:30,114 --> 00:27:31,412
Listen to me calmly.

467
00:27:32,130 --> 00:27:32,787
Tell me.

468
00:27:33,995 --> 00:27:37,828
There's a vacancy for a nanny at the
Collector's house on the next street.

469
00:27:38,716 --> 00:27:39,703
Salary is Rs. 15,000.

470
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:44,537
Until our problems are solved,
I'll do that job.

471
00:27:45,325 --> 00:27:46,203
Don't say no.

472
00:28:02,481 --> 00:28:04,474
[Thunder rumbles]

473
00:28:07,849 --> 00:28:10,703
[chantings]

474
00:28:11,245 --> 00:28:11,995
Venkatramana.

475
00:28:12,703 --> 00:28:13,580
Bye.

476
00:28:14,787 --> 00:28:16,428
-Be careful.
-Okay, sir.

477
00:28:17,245 --> 00:28:18,232
Sleep carefully.

478
00:28:19,263 --> 00:28:23,453
[chantings]

479
00:28:24,432 --> 00:28:29,995
[chantings]

480
00:28:38,940 --> 00:28:42,890
Everyone aspires to live a better
life than the people around them.

481
00:28:44,284 --> 00:28:46,276
But I wish I could die.

482
00:28:48,370 --> 00:28:49,522
I am tired, God.

483
00:28:49,721 --> 00:28:50,904
[Thunder rumbles]

484
00:28:51,703 --> 00:28:53,495
As a son, I couldn't do
anything for my father.

485
00:28:54,370 --> 00:28:56,166
As a father, I couldn't do
anything for my children.

486
00:28:57,455 --> 00:28:59,703
As a husband, I couldn't do anything for
Padmavathi.

487
00:29:00,444 --> 00:29:02,940
[Thunder rumbles]

488
00:29:03,397 --> 00:29:05,576
I used to wake up to your
Suprabhata hymn every day.

489
00:29:06,725 --> 00:29:08,453
Please don't let me wake up tomorrow, God.

490
00:29:12,162 --> 00:29:17,330
At least my family will live happily
with the money they get from my death.

491
00:29:22,662 --> 00:29:24,489
You haven't done anything
for me until now.

492
00:29:26,540 --> 00:29:32,002
Please stop this tired heart
and do me a favor, God.

493
00:29:32,798 --> 00:29:36,338
[Thunder rumbles]

494
00:29:40,931 --> 00:29:45,630
[Venkata Ramana sobbing]

495
00:29:54,957 --> 00:29:59,211
[Thunder rumbles]

496
00:30:02,586 --> 00:30:06,278
[Sanskrit]

497
00:31:51,328 --> 00:31:52,162
Who are you, sir?

498
00:31:52,620 --> 00:31:54,120
Who I am isn't important.

499
00:31:54,937 --> 00:31:57,120
Tell me,
what problem is making you want to die?

500
00:31:58,537 --> 00:31:59,995
Why are you looking at me like that?
Tell me.

501
00:32:00,453 --> 00:32:01,995
If I can, I'll solve it.

502
00:32:02,494 --> 00:32:04,191
Are you God, to solve my problems?

503
00:32:04,703 --> 00:32:05,328
May be.

504
00:32:05,662 --> 00:32:06,578
Consider me as God.

505
00:32:06,787 --> 00:32:07,703
I don't want to talk to him.

506
00:32:07,995 --> 00:32:12,245
Then consider me your friend and
ask me what you would ask God.

507
00:32:12,479 --> 00:32:13,120
Then listen to me.

508
00:32:13,787 --> 00:32:15,319
I am praying to you every day.

509
00:32:15,703 --> 00:32:16,620
But you drove me into debt.

510
00:32:16,979 --> 00:32:17,851
Answer me.

511
00:32:19,453 --> 00:32:22,979
When Goddess Lakshmi comes
home and knocks on the door,

512
00:32:23,162 --> 00:32:26,540
you should catch her quickly
and lock her in a locker.

513
00:32:26,620 --> 00:32:28,997
When did Goddess Lakshmi ever
come to my home or my locker?

514
00:32:29,370 --> 00:32:32,620
When you were running a
tiffin center in Yousufguda.

515
00:32:32,870 --> 00:32:37,620
Your cash box used to be piled up
like the offering box in Tirupati.

516
00:32:37,959 --> 00:32:39,975
Unsatisfied with what you had,

517
00:32:40,219 --> 00:32:44,990
you borrowed money at 4%
interest out of greed,

518
00:32:45,318 --> 00:32:47,620
started a hotel, and ended up insolvent.

519
00:32:48,468 --> 00:32:51,287
Despite being God,
I'm struggling to repay the interest.

520
00:32:51,495 --> 00:32:52,218
So?

521
00:32:52,787 --> 00:32:55,623
Would you turn my happy
life into a miserable one?

522
00:32:55,827 --> 00:32:57,665
Fine. Until now,
I spoke to you considering you God.

523
00:32:57,745 --> 00:32:58,328
Bye.

524
00:32:58,630 --> 00:32:59,745
Wait, wait.

525
00:32:59,953 --> 00:33:00,620
Listen to me.

526
00:33:00,828 --> 00:33:01,787
I won't wait, and I won't listen.

527
00:33:02,078 --> 00:33:03,946
Why are you so angry?

528
00:33:04,237 --> 00:33:07,703
Tell me, as if Lord Venkateswara were
standing before you, what do you want?

529
00:33:07,995 --> 00:33:08,745
I have asked you many times.

530
00:33:09,162 --> 00:33:09,662
No use.

531
00:33:09,955 --> 00:33:10,578
Will it happen now?

532
00:33:10,959 --> 00:33:16,120
[speaking in Sanskrit]

533
00:33:16,817 --> 00:33:18,870
There is no success without trying.

534
00:33:19,461 --> 00:33:21,328
There is no fortune without trying.

535
00:33:22,546 --> 00:33:25,245
Tell me now, what do you want?

536
00:33:25,686 --> 00:33:26,287
What should I ask?

537
00:33:26,787 --> 00:33:29,539
Not even all the jewels worn by Lord
Venkateswara could clear my debt.

538
00:33:29,914 --> 00:33:31,328
Will he give them to me?

539
00:33:32,070 --> 00:33:32,670
Tell me.

540
00:33:32,912 --> 00:33:34,142
Go away, man.

541
00:33:40,412 --> 00:33:42,370
Venkata Ramana...

542
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:44,078
What is it, Venkata Ramana?

543
00:33:44,912 --> 00:33:47,370
You asked for jewels, right?

544
00:33:47,651 --> 00:33:50,117
Come...

545
00:33:57,683 --> 00:34:00,245
Come...

546
00:34:11,634 --> 00:34:16,097
[Sanskrit]

547
00:34:59,870 --> 00:35:01,094
You look good.

548
00:35:01,870 --> 00:35:03,912
You look like Lord
Venkateshwara with a mustache.

549
00:35:05,369 --> 00:35:06,245
Go home now.

550
00:35:22,113 --> 00:35:24,757
[Sanskrit]

551
00:36:03,345 --> 00:36:05,717
[Music]

552
00:36:26,453 --> 00:36:27,531
What is this?

553
00:36:27,859 --> 00:36:30,540
You said you wouldn't say his
name or visit his temple, right?

554
00:36:30,944 --> 00:36:32,995
Why have you come wearing his getup?

555
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:36,287
Though Ramadasu castrated Lord Rama,

556
00:36:36,606 --> 00:36:39,828
saying,
"With whose property are you enjoying? ",

557
00:36:40,234 --> 00:36:42,620
wasn't Ramadasu Lord Rama's devotee?

558
00:36:42,953 --> 00:36:48,078
Though I kept the Lord in the attic,
am I not the Lord's devotee?

559
00:36:49,788 --> 00:36:51,550
Having climbed his
hill a hundred times,

560
00:36:53,078 --> 00:36:54,995
don't I have the right to keep
him in the attic just once?

561
00:36:56,238 --> 00:36:57,495
Think about it, my family members.

562
00:36:57,828 --> 00:36:59,135
We will think about it.

563
00:36:59,453 --> 00:37:01,123
By the way,
who gave you the jewels, brother?

564
00:37:01,203 --> 00:37:01,787
Lord.

565
00:37:02,078 --> 00:37:03,457
Who? You mean Arvind Swamy?

566
00:37:03,691 --> 00:37:04,694
Stop it!

567
00:37:05,594 --> 00:37:07,328
Lord Venkateshwar.

568
00:37:08,116 --> 00:37:09,453
But he came in civilian dress.

569
00:37:10,787 --> 00:37:13,162
Earlier at the temple,
we both had a big argument.

570
00:37:13,242 --> 00:37:14,370
[unison]: Oh!

571
00:37:14,706 --> 00:37:15,412
I won.

572
00:37:15,828 --> 00:37:16,553
[unison]: Aha!

573
00:37:16,745 --> 00:37:17,953
He asked me what I wanted.

574
00:37:18,245 --> 00:37:18,912
[unison]: Ah!

575
00:37:19,150 --> 00:37:20,537
-I asked him for his jewelry.
-[unison]: Ah!

576
00:37:21,194 --> 00:37:21,745
That's all.

577
00:37:22,078 --> 00:37:23,912
He himself adorned me with jewelry.

578
00:37:24,287 --> 00:37:25,506
[unison]: Oho!

579
00:37:25,909 --> 00:37:28,328
He came over and twisted my moustache.

580
00:37:28,787 --> 00:37:33,043
He said, "You look like Lord Venkateshwara
with a mustache. You look good."

581
00:37:33,717 --> 00:37:34,703
His madness increased.

582
00:37:35,067 --> 00:37:37,453
On my way home, I looked back.

583
00:37:37,720 --> 00:37:38,620
[unison]: Ah!

584
00:37:39,736 --> 00:37:40,412
I saw Vaikuntam.

585
00:37:41,930 --> 00:37:42,745
I saw Lord Venkateshwara.

586
00:37:44,620 --> 00:37:45,245
Oh!

587
00:37:45,492 --> 00:37:48,870
[chanting Lord Venkateswara's name]

588
00:37:49,196 --> 00:37:50,995
Why are you talking like a mad man?

589
00:37:51,412 --> 00:37:52,936
Did you step on an evil-eye
lemon or something?

590
00:37:53,578 --> 00:37:55,287
Father-in-law, I am worried.

591
00:37:55,745 --> 00:37:57,370
You funny-faced woman!

592
00:37:57,605 --> 00:37:58,915
You should get a check-up at
Apollo Hospital, brother-in-law.

593
00:37:58,995 --> 00:37:59,995
The situation might get out of hand.

594
00:38:00,352 --> 00:38:01,037
Don't you believe me?

595
00:38:04,412 --> 00:38:04,995
No.

596
00:38:05,368 --> 00:38:08,406
I swear on Lord Tirupati Vekateswara,
Srisailam Mallanna, Vemulawada Rajanna,

597
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:11,238
Goddess Kanchi Kamakshi,
Madurai Meenakshi, Kasi Vishalakshi,

598
00:38:11,491 --> 00:38:14,457
Goddess Peddamma, Yellamma, Poleramma,
Ankalamma, Nukalamma, Mavullamma,

599
00:38:14,537 --> 00:38:17,332
Goddess Bejawada Kanaka Durgamma,
Lord Yadagirigutta Sri Lakshmi Narasimha,

600
00:38:17,489 --> 00:38:21,844
Lord Palani Subramanya,
Kondagattu Anjaneya,

601
00:38:21,924 --> 00:38:24,120
Lord Kanipaka Varasiddhi Vinayaka.

602
00:38:24,324 --> 00:38:25,815
I swear on the 33 categories of deities.

603
00:38:26,077 --> 00:38:28,912
Lord Venkateswara himself
adorned me with this jewellery.

604
00:38:29,328 --> 00:38:31,617
This jewellery and that
jewellery are the same.

605
00:38:32,370 --> 00:38:32,995
This is the truth.

606
00:38:33,492 --> 00:38:35,245
Any doubt?

607
00:38:36,745 --> 00:38:37,620
There is no doubt.

608
00:38:38,078 --> 00:38:39,783
His brain seems completely disconnected.

609
00:38:40,655 --> 00:38:41,703
I will manage.

610
00:38:41,995 --> 00:38:42,953
You wait, father-in-law.

611
00:38:46,505 --> 00:38:47,287
-Hubby.
-Hmm.

612
00:38:47,620 --> 00:38:48,912
These are all gold jewellery.

613
00:38:49,327 --> 00:38:50,370
These are bestowed by God.

614
00:38:50,745 --> 00:38:52,439
Not only I, but all of us believe in it.

615
00:38:52,703 --> 00:38:54,891
You are very tired after arguing with God.

616
00:38:54,971 --> 00:38:55,458
Yes.

617
00:38:55,620 --> 00:38:56,953
First, we will keep
all this jewellery here.

618
00:38:57,764 --> 00:38:58,828
Take a bath.

619
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:00,914
We will talk in the morning.

620
00:39:26,555 --> 00:39:27,120
Brother.

621
00:39:39,549 --> 00:39:40,287
Venkat Ramana.

622
00:39:41,412 --> 00:39:42,453
These are all gilded jewellery.

623
00:39:43,402 --> 00:39:44,949
Pack them and give them in the temple.

624
00:39:46,955 --> 00:39:47,745
How were you back then?

625
00:39:47,939 --> 00:39:48,828
How did you become like this?

626
00:39:50,162 --> 00:39:50,745
Yes, brother.

627
00:39:50,912 --> 00:39:52,365
When you spoke like that last night,

628
00:39:52,684 --> 00:39:54,943
we were all afraid you
might have gone mad.

629
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:58,995
Why do you think he might have gone mad?
He has gone mad, confirmed.

630
00:40:01,245 --> 00:40:02,037
Look at that pose.

631
00:40:02,668 --> 00:40:05,078
Pose like the head of the
theatre arts department.

632
00:40:07,328 --> 00:40:08,870
Brother-in-law, Did you see that colour?

633
00:40:09,120 --> 00:40:10,662
Even Dubai gold doesn't have that colour.

634
00:40:11,077 --> 00:40:12,995
I worked at a rolled gold
shop in Chilakalpudi.

635
00:40:13,203 --> 00:40:14,203
I have a lot of experience.

636
00:40:14,412 --> 00:40:15,078
It's rolled gold.

637
00:40:31,870 --> 00:40:34,711
As everyone says, are these gilded
jewellery or gold jewellery?

638
00:40:38,412 --> 00:40:38,953
Hubby.

639
00:40:48,620 --> 00:40:50,498
Is this gold or rolled gold?

640
00:40:50,705 --> 00:40:51,373
It's Manappuram gold.

641
00:40:51,530 --> 00:40:52,758
Check how much it costs.

642
00:40:54,718 --> 00:40:55,453
Brother, look at this.

643
00:41:16,953 --> 00:41:18,040
This diamond bracelet...

644
00:41:18,120 --> 00:41:20,078
Brother, its value is in crores.

645
00:41:20,453 --> 00:41:21,390
We can't buy it.

646
00:41:21,765 --> 00:41:23,171
Wait, I will manage.

647
00:41:24,634 --> 00:41:25,665
I will give you Rs. 3 lakhs.

648
00:41:25,745 --> 00:41:26,328
Sell it.

649
00:41:30,245 --> 00:41:30,995
Rs. 3 lakhs?

650
00:41:32,203 --> 00:41:33,521
I will give you Rs. 5 lakhs.

651
00:41:34,374 --> 00:41:35,120
Rs. 5 lakhs?

652
00:41:36,408 --> 00:41:37,608
Finally Rs. 10 lakhs.

653
00:41:38,892 --> 00:41:40,373
Rs. 10 lakhs...

654
00:41:40,861 --> 00:41:42,483
Wait a minute. I will think about it.

655
00:41:43,162 --> 00:41:44,037
Okay, think about it.

656
00:41:47,328 --> 00:41:48,811
The diamond crown costs Rs. 50 lakhs.

657
00:41:51,914 --> 00:41:54,895
The conch and discus
each cost Rs. 35 lakhs.

658
00:41:57,620 --> 00:41:59,695
The armlets cost Rs. 45 lakhs.

659
00:42:00,474 --> 00:42:01,870
The holy basil rosary costs Rs.70 lakhs.

660
00:42:02,578 --> 00:42:04,287
The nine stones cost Rs. 90 lakhs.

661
00:42:04,870 --> 00:42:06,578
The Moon garland costs Rs. 85 lakhs.

662
00:42:07,402 --> 00:42:09,464
In total, it is around
Rs. 4 to Rs. 5 crores.

663
00:42:11,883 --> 00:42:13,762
-What is your account balance?
-Rs. 3 crores.

664
00:42:13,842 --> 00:42:14,495
Withdraw all the money.

665
00:42:15,755 --> 00:42:17,162
Hey, Venkata Ramana, wait. Wait.

666
00:42:17,902 --> 00:42:19,064
Oh no! He is leaving.

667
00:42:23,631 --> 00:42:24,662
[Brakes squeal]
- Hey!

668
00:42:26,359 --> 00:42:29,331
I thought I gave birth to a son, but I
didn't think he would be a crazy one.

669
00:42:34,537 --> 00:42:35,453
What, man? Are you begging now?

670
00:42:35,856 --> 00:42:37,162
Perhaps he found out it's rolled gold.

671
00:42:37,572 --> 00:42:38,787
All of you, keep quiet.

672
00:42:39,287 --> 00:42:43,600
After hearing the big news,
no one will know who will fall where.

673
00:42:43,946 --> 00:42:44,620
Be ready.

674
00:42:44,893 --> 00:42:45,828
By the way, Where is my God?

675
00:42:46,084 --> 00:42:48,453
Lord Govinda... Lord Govinda...

676
00:42:50,950 --> 00:42:51,953
Are you in the attic, Lord Govinda?

677
00:42:52,206 --> 00:42:52,995
I'm coming.

678
00:42:53,662 --> 00:42:54,495
I'll bring you down, God.

679
00:42:56,425 --> 00:42:57,328
Lord Govinda...

680
00:43:02,620 --> 00:43:04,412
Whether on a hill or in an attic,
God remains God.

681
00:43:22,995 --> 00:43:24,620
I'm scared seeing your condition,
brother-in-law.

682
00:43:26,828 --> 00:43:27,537
You should be scared.

683
00:43:27,912 --> 00:43:30,245
From now on, I'm a multimillionaire.

684
00:43:30,453 --> 00:43:31,328
Will you take me to Apollo Hospital?

685
00:43:31,537 --> 00:43:32,791
I'll bring Apollo home.

686
00:43:34,037 --> 00:43:34,745
Padma...

687
00:43:36,016 --> 00:43:37,078
From now on, I'm the king.

688
00:43:37,620 --> 00:43:38,453
You're the queen.

689
00:43:38,995 --> 00:43:41,800
Let's dance rock and roll and disco.

690
00:43:43,370 --> 00:43:44,120
Move aside.

691
00:43:50,953 --> 00:43:51,745
Where is the jewellery?

692
00:43:52,662 --> 00:43:53,495
Where have you kept the jewellery?

693
00:43:53,703 --> 00:43:54,578
Did you keep it in the cupboard?

694
00:44:00,453 --> 00:44:01,203
It's not in the cupboard.

695
00:44:01,995 --> 00:44:02,828
It's not here either.

696
00:44:03,078 --> 00:44:04,120
Did you keep them under the cot?

697
00:44:06,912 --> 00:44:07,495
It's not here either.

698
00:44:08,162 --> 00:44:08,953
Where did you keep them?

699
00:44:10,995 --> 00:44:12,587
Where did you keep the jewellery?

700
00:44:13,537 --> 00:44:14,078
I mean...

701
00:44:14,247 --> 00:44:17,245
You've been acting weird
since you got the jewellery.

702
00:44:17,745 --> 00:44:18,412
So?

703
00:44:18,912 --> 00:44:21,691
-Everyone in the house came to a decision.
-Then?

704
00:44:22,120 --> 00:44:24,203
All the jewellery was packed in a sack.

705
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:25,169
After that?

706
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:35,370
[chanting Lord Venkateswara's names]

707
00:44:37,085 --> 00:44:38,245
Oh, God!

708
00:44:38,325 --> 00:44:39,245
Brother...

709
00:44:39,578 --> 00:44:40,287
Brother...

710
00:44:40,544 --> 00:44:42,828
-[Heart pounding]
-Brother-in-law...

711
00:44:43,572 --> 00:44:44,412
Dear...

712
00:44:51,800 --> 00:44:53,203
-You...
-Brother, stop.

713
00:44:53,450 --> 00:44:54,120
Brother, stop.

714
00:44:55,078 --> 00:44:57,866
I was planning to buy a five-bedroom
villa beside Gandipet Lake.

715
00:44:58,044 --> 00:45:00,123
But you took all the jewellery
and threw it into the lake.

716
00:45:00,293 --> 00:45:01,953
You wicked woman.

717
00:45:02,347 --> 00:45:04,912
Why are you fighting for
the gilded jewellery, brother?

718
00:45:06,328 --> 00:45:07,745
It's not gilded jewellery.
It's gold jewellery.

719
00:45:08,543 --> 00:45:09,745
24-carat gold.

720
00:45:10,803 --> 00:45:12,370
We don't even have money to buy carrots.

721
00:45:12,620 --> 00:45:13,912
How can we get 24-carat gold?

722
00:45:14,206 --> 00:45:15,453
You fool, I will...

723
00:45:15,678 --> 00:45:16,995
-Leave him... Leave him.
-Brother-in-law...

724
00:45:17,768 --> 00:45:20,703
For your misfortune, even a Rs.
5 coin looks like a gold coin to you.

725
00:45:20,912 --> 00:45:21,537
Leave it.

726
00:45:21,703 --> 00:45:22,415
Relax.

727
00:45:22,495 --> 00:45:23,495
How can I?

728
00:45:23,995 --> 00:45:25,745
She is a dimwit.
You could have stopped her.

729
00:45:27,163 --> 00:45:29,619
He was the one who gave us the idea.

730
00:45:30,037 --> 00:45:30,979
Move aside.

731
00:45:31,288 --> 00:45:32,703
You, old man.

732
00:45:36,031 --> 00:45:36,995
Hey, come on.

733
00:45:37,075 --> 00:45:38,870
-Where did you throw it? Come.
-Brother-in-law...

734
00:45:47,203 --> 00:45:47,912
Get down.

735
00:45:49,995 --> 00:45:50,578
Come.

736
00:45:52,081 --> 00:45:53,412
Where did you throw it? Tell me clearly.

737
00:45:53,675 --> 00:45:54,870
-Tell me.
-I don't know.

738
00:45:55,306 --> 00:45:58,537
I closed my eyes,
spun around, and threw it.

739
00:45:58,617 --> 00:46:00,725
I will cut you into pieces.

740
00:46:01,747 --> 00:46:02,537
Move aside.

741
00:46:03,495 --> 00:46:06,162
-Hubby!
-Lord Govinda!

742
00:46:08,870 --> 00:46:10,037
You can't swim at all.

743
00:46:19,412 --> 00:46:20,495
-Hubby...
-Where did you throw it?

744
00:46:20,703 --> 00:46:21,912
I can't find it, fool.

745
00:46:22,165 --> 00:46:24,328
Okay, I am a fool. You come out first.

746
00:46:28,745 --> 00:46:29,707
-Here.
-Stop.

747
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:31,162
-Stop.
-Father-in-law...

748
00:46:31,512 --> 00:46:32,627
-What happened? Brother-in-law.
- Look at him.

749
00:46:32,828 --> 00:46:34,793
Your son jumped into the lake,
unable to face his debts.

750
00:46:35,495 --> 00:46:36,987
-Brother...
-Brother-in-law...

751
00:46:37,245 --> 00:46:39,256
-Venkata Ramana...
-Brother.

752
00:46:40,203 --> 00:46:40,787
Father-in-law...

753
00:46:41,203 --> 00:46:42,078
Father-in-law, jump in.

754
00:46:42,328 --> 00:46:44,370
I have knee pain.
I can't jump. I can't swim.

755
00:46:45,287 --> 00:46:47,759
-Brother-in-law...
-Venkata Ramana...

756
00:46:47,918 --> 00:46:48,870
Forgive me, Father-in-law.

757
00:46:50,578 --> 00:46:52,653
-Oh no!
-Oh no! She pushed me.

758
00:47:09,161 --> 00:47:10,080
[Tea slurping]

759
00:47:12,799 --> 00:47:13,745
Sorry.

760
00:47:15,578 --> 00:47:17,120
Dad, why did you jump?

761
00:47:17,370 --> 00:47:18,623
Why did I jump?

762
00:47:18,703 --> 00:47:20,495
I jumped because my
daughter-in-law kicked me.

763
00:47:24,012 --> 00:47:25,370
Hey, why did you jump?

764
00:47:25,568 --> 00:47:27,412
Just like Father-in-law, I was kicked too.

765
00:47:27,865 --> 00:47:30,781
Is this a Kumbh Mela, that we're all
taking a dip in the water together?

766
00:47:32,037 --> 00:47:34,082
You could have skipped paying the debts.

767
00:47:34,162 --> 00:47:35,203
Why did you jump into the dam?

768
00:47:35,412 --> 00:47:37,412
Hey, we take loans so
we can avoid paying them.

769
00:47:37,625 --> 00:47:40,370
I took several loans in Tamil Nadu,
came to Telangana, and settled here.

770
00:47:40,550 --> 00:47:41,620
Has anyone touched me?

771
00:47:42,453 --> 00:47:43,859
Hey, who's in the house?

772
00:47:48,078 --> 00:47:49,120
Who among you is Venkata Ramana?

773
00:47:49,828 --> 00:47:50,412
It's me.

774
00:47:50,492 --> 00:47:52,078
The SI has called for you. Come.

775
00:47:53,562 --> 00:47:54,245
You wait here.

776
00:47:55,803 --> 00:47:56,453
Let's go.

777
00:47:59,038 --> 00:47:59,745
-Ouch!
-Tell me.

778
00:48:00,266 --> 00:48:02,912
I won't let you leave today until you
tell the truth. Will you tell me or not?

779
00:48:03,360 --> 00:48:04,757
-Tell me.
-Don't hit me, sir.

780
00:48:04,837 --> 00:48:06,787
-I plead with you, sir. Please let me go.
-I'm giving you a break.

781
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:10,245
-Close the cell.
-Okay, sir.

782
00:48:12,396 --> 00:48:12,915
[Clears throat]

783
00:48:12,995 --> 00:48:15,120
I asked you to make a love call
last night. Why didn't you?

784
00:48:15,328 --> 00:48:16,328
My husband is next to me.

785
00:48:16,828 --> 00:48:17,921
That's the fun.

786
00:48:18,213 --> 00:48:19,162
You should do it then.

787
00:48:19,578 --> 00:48:23,164
You know, right?
I'm a big psycho in matters of romance.

788
00:48:23,856 --> 00:48:25,575
-I think he's a terrible guy.
-Terrible to the core.

789
00:48:26,370 --> 00:48:27,495
Sir, someone has come.

790
00:48:30,245 --> 00:48:31,537
Hey, you come here.

791
00:48:33,262 --> 00:48:34,162
-Greetings, sir.
-Hmm.

792
00:48:35,370 --> 00:48:35,953
Sit down.

793
00:48:37,262 --> 00:48:37,995
Sit down, man.

794
00:48:39,578 --> 00:48:40,328
Hey!

795
00:48:41,414 --> 00:48:42,245
You sit down, sir.

796
00:48:43,953 --> 00:48:45,620
You are very arrogant.

797
00:48:48,755 --> 00:48:54,453
By the way, I heard that you stole
a gold bracelet from a gold shop.

798
00:48:55,328 --> 00:48:56,203
I didn't steal it, sir.

799
00:48:57,370 --> 00:48:58,037
This is mine, sir.

800
00:49:03,977 --> 00:49:06,870
You look like a man
too poor to buy snacks.

801
00:49:07,393 --> 00:49:08,745
Where did you get the
gold bracelette from?

802
00:49:09,242 --> 00:49:09,995
Who gave it to you?

803
00:49:10,453 --> 00:49:11,245
Lord gave it to me, sir.

804
00:49:11,999 --> 00:49:12,620
Lord?

805
00:49:13,287 --> 00:49:14,912
Is Venu Swami the astrologer?

806
00:49:15,437 --> 00:49:16,896
Lord Venkateswara

807
00:49:17,245 --> 00:49:18,831
You mean Lord Venkateswara?

808
00:49:19,787 --> 00:49:20,787
He was in civilian attire, sir.

809
00:49:21,245 --> 00:49:23,120
I had an argument with him last night.

810
00:49:25,145 --> 00:49:26,203
He asked me what I wanted.

811
00:49:27,245 --> 00:49:28,453
I asked him for his jewels, sir.

812
00:49:28,745 --> 00:49:29,495
Did he give it to you?

813
00:49:29,828 --> 00:49:31,372
He himself adorned me with them, sir.

814
00:49:36,912 --> 00:49:37,620
Not only that, sir.

815
00:49:38,037 --> 00:49:38,953
He twisteded my moustache.

816
00:49:39,495 --> 00:49:42,037
And he said that I look like Lord
Venkateswara with a mustache.

817
00:49:45,120 --> 00:49:46,120
-Sir!
-Hmm.

818
00:49:46,453 --> 00:49:50,203
When I turned back while walking home,
I saw Vaikuntam, sir.

819
00:49:53,703 --> 00:49:55,787
Lord Venkateswara appeared before me.

820
00:50:04,078 --> 00:50:05,370
This is not a theft case.

821
00:50:06,328 --> 00:50:07,287
This is a case of mental illness.

822
00:50:08,078 --> 00:50:10,037
I don't care if he is a mad or a cook.
That bracelet is mine.

823
00:50:10,245 --> 00:50:11,479
-Give me the bracelet.
-Okay.

824
00:50:22,495 --> 00:50:23,037
Bye, sir.

825
00:50:23,287 --> 00:50:24,245
-Ah!
-My bracelet, sir.

826
00:50:24,745 --> 00:50:25,370
Stop him.

827
00:50:25,745 --> 00:50:26,745
-Catch him.
-Hey!

828
00:50:27,578 --> 00:50:28,162
Catch him.

829
00:50:28,537 --> 00:50:29,287
Don't let him go.

830
00:50:35,703 --> 00:50:36,328
Hey!

831
00:50:37,495 --> 00:50:37,995
That's it.

832
00:50:40,537 --> 00:50:41,328
Lord Govinda!

833
00:50:43,537 --> 00:50:45,287
Hey, take the bracelet from his hand.

834
00:50:45,652 --> 00:50:48,690
[Sanskrit]

835
00:50:56,328 --> 00:50:56,953
Let it go.

836
00:51:01,453 --> 00:51:02,203
Let it go.

837
00:51:02,370 --> 00:51:03,245
Sir, do something.

838
00:51:19,412 --> 00:51:21,120
I heard a metal sound when I hit you.

839
00:51:21,578 --> 00:51:22,495
Is there a rod inside?

840
00:51:22,929 --> 00:51:24,828
-Is it the power of the rod?
-It's the power of God.

841
00:51:24,995 --> 00:51:26,245
Show him our police power.

842
00:51:26,412 --> 00:51:27,120
Hit him.

843
00:51:27,406 --> 00:51:27,995
Hit him.

844
00:51:38,325 --> 00:51:39,745
Hey, she is my girl.

845
00:51:39,947 --> 00:51:40,537
Damn!

846
00:51:44,746 --> 00:51:45,412
Ah!

847
00:51:45,662 --> 00:51:46,412
Hey!

848
00:51:56,801 --> 00:51:57,370
Hey!

849
00:52:03,203 --> 00:52:04,370
-Hey, fatso.
-Sir.

850
00:52:04,537 --> 00:52:06,537
-Bring the coconut knife.
-Yes, sir.

851
00:52:06,745 --> 00:52:07,287
Go!

852
00:52:07,367 --> 00:52:09,428
I'll take the bracelet,
even if I have to cut off his hand.

853
00:52:23,412 --> 00:52:24,245
Hit him.

854
00:52:24,828 --> 00:52:25,995
Hey!

855
00:52:26,412 --> 00:52:29,120
Where are you going with the knife, fatso?

856
00:52:29,453 --> 00:52:30,120
Go away.

857
00:52:30,870 --> 00:52:31,537
Hey!

858
00:52:31,745 --> 00:52:32,412
[wailing in pain]

859
00:52:34,445 --> 00:52:35,662
Stop... Stop.

860
00:52:40,218 --> 00:52:40,912
Take it.

861
00:52:44,370 --> 00:52:45,162
Stop.

862
00:52:45,870 --> 00:52:49,698
Hey, even if I have to kill you,
I'll take that bracelet today.

863
00:52:50,023 --> 00:52:52,620
How dare you hit a policeman?

864
00:52:52,828 --> 00:52:54,120
-Hubby.
-You are finished.

865
00:52:54,287 --> 00:52:55,162
-Hubby.
-You are finished.

866
00:52:58,203 --> 00:52:58,995
-Hubby.
-Why did you come here?

867
00:52:59,828 --> 00:53:00,537
What did he do?

868
00:53:00,745 --> 00:53:01,827
Why are you hitting him?

869
00:53:03,912 --> 00:53:05,995
-Who is she?
-His wife.

870
00:53:06,620 --> 00:53:07,328
Is it?

871
00:53:09,211 --> 00:53:13,092
File an extramarital affair case
against her and the man in the cell.

872
00:53:13,320 --> 00:53:14,662
Put her behind bars.

873
00:53:21,654 --> 00:53:25,178
[Sanskrit]

874
00:53:39,459 --> 00:53:40,870
I don't understand you, God.

875
00:54:07,448 --> 00:54:08,078
Auto rikshaw!

876
00:54:16,578 --> 00:54:17,162
Start.

877
00:54:17,370 --> 00:54:17,953
Come.

878
00:54:18,620 --> 00:54:19,245
You go.

879
00:54:19,662 --> 00:54:21,245
No, you also come.

880
00:54:21,415 --> 00:54:22,328
I am telling you to go.

881
00:54:22,691 --> 00:54:23,787
No... No.

882
00:54:23,995 --> 00:54:24,662
God!

883
00:54:26,745 --> 00:54:27,287
Start.

884
00:54:56,129 --> 00:54:59,828
If a woman works hard,
she can earn a lot of money.

885
00:55:00,789 --> 00:55:02,583
Get the school fees, daddy.

886
00:55:03,707 --> 00:55:07,675
There's a vacancy for a nanny at the
Collector's house on the next street.

887
00:55:09,081 --> 00:55:12,745
File an extramarital affair case
against her and the man in the cell.

888
00:55:17,707 --> 00:55:20,647
[Lord Hanuman Chalisa]

889
00:55:35,685 --> 00:55:36,766
[Brakes squeal]

890
00:55:43,037 --> 00:55:44,620
You can't even hit properly.
What kind of driver are you?

891
00:55:47,203 --> 00:55:48,453
Venkata Ramana.

892
00:55:49,285 --> 00:55:50,485
What is your problem?

893
00:55:50,995 --> 00:55:51,995
God, is it you?

894
00:55:55,307 --> 00:55:57,162
I have a big issue to settle with you.
Get down.

895
00:55:57,457 --> 00:55:58,870
-Me?
-You only.

896
00:55:59,230 --> 00:56:01,495
My life has fallen apart
like the stock market.

897
00:56:02,037 --> 00:56:03,467
Because of you. Get down.

898
00:56:04,602 --> 00:56:07,328
-You're being too lenient.
-Get down.

899
00:56:07,703 --> 00:56:10,453
I can't scold you because
you are a devotee.

900
00:56:10,742 --> 00:56:12,787
Devotee is my weakness.

901
00:56:13,162 --> 00:56:14,787
God, what is this cheating?

902
00:56:16,245 --> 00:56:17,370
You asked for jewellery.

903
00:56:17,813 --> 00:56:18,537
I gave it.

904
00:56:18,753 --> 00:56:20,332
-What is cheating in this?
-You gave it.

905
00:56:20,620 --> 00:56:21,828
You also took it back, right?

906
00:56:22,537 --> 00:56:24,078
Hello, hello, hello.

907
00:56:25,120 --> 00:56:27,078
It is my responsibility to give you.

908
00:56:27,489 --> 00:56:30,287
It is your inefficiency not to save it.

909
00:56:30,787 --> 00:56:31,787
I am a fool.

910
00:56:32,078 --> 00:56:33,287
My wife is a big fool.

911
00:56:33,870 --> 00:56:37,912
She immersed all the jewellery in the
lake, like immersing Lord Vinayaka.

912
00:56:37,992 --> 00:56:39,912
Oh no!

913
00:56:40,288 --> 00:56:41,453
Don't act, God.

914
00:56:42,287 --> 00:56:44,370
Because of you, I have become a fool.

915
00:56:44,620 --> 00:56:47,787
Not only me, all the middle class families
are becoming fools.

916
00:56:48,287 --> 00:56:49,953
All the rich are happy.

917
00:56:50,245 --> 00:56:51,203
The poor are unhappy.

918
00:56:51,912 --> 00:56:53,078
All the bad people are happy.

919
00:56:53,870 --> 00:56:54,745
The good people are unhappy.

920
00:56:55,078 --> 00:56:56,203
All the currepted people are happy.

921
00:56:56,655 --> 00:56:57,693
The honest people are unhappy.

922
00:56:58,203 --> 00:56:59,453
What is this, God?

923
00:57:00,828 --> 00:57:01,703
Venkata Ramana...

924
00:57:11,714 --> 00:57:13,787
[Sanskrit sloka]

925
00:57:14,612 --> 00:57:19,787
[Sanskrit sloka]

926
00:57:20,330 --> 00:57:21,120
It means...

927
00:57:22,601 --> 00:57:24,578
The result of a man's sins...

928
00:57:25,495 --> 00:57:28,537
...must be experienced in this world.

929
00:57:29,908 --> 00:57:34,783
The criminals and murderers
you mentioned will not be happy.

930
00:57:36,091 --> 00:57:39,245
They will be punished for their sins.

931
00:57:41,287 --> 00:57:42,120
Venkata Ramana...

932
00:57:42,751 --> 00:57:44,787
I will show you a way. Come with me.

933
00:57:54,537 --> 00:57:56,745
Why did he leave me halfway after
saying he would show me the way?

934
00:57:56,978 --> 00:57:57,578
Lord Govinda...

935
00:57:58,308 --> 00:57:58,953
Lord Govinda...

936
00:58:01,120 --> 00:58:02,093
Where did you go, God?

937
00:58:03,660 --> 00:58:04,245
Lord Govinda...

938
00:58:04,980 --> 00:58:05,620
Lord Govinda...

939
00:58:05,870 --> 00:58:06,453
Lord Govinda...

940
00:58:21,627 --> 00:58:25,984
[Sanskrit]

941
00:58:35,078 --> 00:58:35,995
[God] 'Venkata Ramana...'

942
00:58:38,816 --> 00:58:41,453
'Lord Brahma writes the
fate of every human.'

943
00:58:42,578 --> 00:58:46,912
'But I am giving you an opportunity
to write your own fate.'

944
00:58:49,203 --> 00:58:54,537
'This book has 13 pages,
and whatever you write in it will happen.'

945
00:59:01,489 --> 00:59:02,620
'Conditions...'

946
00:59:03,369 --> 00:59:07,037
'In this book, only
one wish must be written in one page.'

947
00:59:07,240 --> 00:59:10,828
'Second one: Do not write against destiny.'

948
00:59:11,045 --> 00:59:14,912
'Third one: Do not write to save the dead.'

949
00:59:15,457 --> 00:59:20,578
'If others get hold of the book,
whatever they write will be fulfilled.'

950
00:59:21,046 --> 00:59:25,120
'Every wish written in the book
must be written with trust.'

951
00:59:25,200 --> 00:59:28,328
'If you write without trust,
the wish will not be fulfilled.'

952
00:59:28,591 --> 00:59:33,582
'In any situation,
the book should not fall on the floor.'

953
00:59:33,770 --> 00:59:37,203
'If it falls, the book will lose its power.'

954
00:59:37,706 --> 00:59:40,370
'If you write against these conditions...'

955
00:59:40,582 --> 00:59:42,245
'The page will burn.'

956
00:59:43,328 --> 00:59:43,953
God...

957
00:59:44,376 --> 00:59:44,981
Lord Govinda...

958
00:59:45,703 --> 00:59:48,733
Hail Lord of the seven hills!

959
00:59:52,620 --> 00:59:53,912
Sir, Why don't you
get in the auto rickshaw?

960
00:59:54,181 --> 00:59:55,245
No, I will walk.

961
00:59:55,435 --> 00:59:56,578
Is it Tirupati to go by walk?

962
00:59:56,775 --> 00:59:57,488
It is Hyderabad, sir.

963
00:59:57,568 --> 00:59:58,828
If all the ladies travel in free buses...

964
00:59:59,143 --> 01:00:00,743
...and men like you walk,

965
01:00:00,912 --> 01:00:01,995
how will auto drivers like me survive?

966
01:00:02,162 --> 01:00:02,787
You come, sir.

967
01:00:03,078 --> 01:00:04,203
-Go away, man.
-You drive well, sir.

968
01:00:04,283 --> 01:00:05,412
I will go slowly. There is AC also.

969
01:00:05,492 --> 01:00:07,290
It is so hot, sir.

970
01:00:07,370 --> 01:00:09,203
How will you walk in the hot sun, sir?
You look fair. You will get tanned.

971
01:00:09,283 --> 01:00:11,802
Get in. You will get tanned.

972
01:00:12,870 --> 01:00:13,704
Who are you?

973
01:00:16,078 --> 01:00:17,578
Sir, my name is Lucky Bhaskar.

974
01:00:18,915 --> 01:00:20,248
I have a terrible flashback.

975
01:00:20,328 --> 01:00:21,434
Do you want to hear it?

976
01:00:21,693 --> 01:00:23,287
Why are you telling your
terrible flash back to me?

977
01:00:23,585 --> 01:00:25,088
Mr. Ambani or Mr. Adani
won't listen to me.

978
01:00:25,168 --> 01:00:26,162
At least, you listen to me.

979
01:00:27,617 --> 01:00:28,287
Okay, tell me.

980
01:00:29,120 --> 01:00:30,493
I used to have 50 auto rikshaws.

981
01:00:31,466 --> 01:00:32,536
I sold all the autos...

982
01:00:32,828 --> 01:00:34,903
and put them in the share market to take
over the country.

983
01:00:35,703 --> 01:00:39,304
I lost everything in the share market,
and I am surviving by driving an auto.

984
01:00:40,342 --> 01:00:41,488
He is more unfortunate than me.

985
01:00:41,745 --> 01:00:42,498
Correct, sir.

986
01:00:42,578 --> 01:00:44,662
No one can change my fate.

987
01:00:45,412 --> 01:00:45,953
Shut up.

988
01:00:46,245 --> 01:00:47,873
Why are you pulling me in your misfortune?

989
01:00:48,083 --> 01:00:49,453
Seeing your face, I felt like it, sir.

990
01:00:49,629 --> 01:00:50,203
I am sorry, sir.

991
01:00:50,537 --> 01:00:51,520
Okay, stop here.

992
01:00:51,780 --> 01:00:52,912
Here... Here.

993
01:00:52,992 --> 01:00:53,957
I stopped, sir.

994
01:00:54,037 --> 01:00:55,866
No matter where I stop,
our misfortune won't change, sir.

995
01:00:55,946 --> 01:00:57,745
Stop saying misfortune.

996
01:00:57,912 --> 01:00:58,578
You will be lucky.

997
01:00:59,531 --> 01:01:00,774
I don't believe you.

998
01:01:15,823 --> 01:01:17,662
Hubby, did you come?

999
01:01:18,007 --> 01:01:19,159
Are you okay?

1000
01:01:19,239 --> 01:01:20,912
Why are you worried?

1001
01:01:21,328 --> 01:01:22,548
Do you know what happened today?

1002
01:01:22,872 --> 01:01:24,703
Book... where is the book?

1003
01:01:24,959 --> 01:01:26,207
What book?

1004
01:01:26,408 --> 01:01:27,412
Lord Venkateswara gave me a book.

1005
01:01:28,037 --> 01:01:29,328
-Wait a minute.
-Hubby.

1006
01:01:29,537 --> 01:01:30,745
Where is this hapless fellow?

1007
01:01:33,068 --> 01:01:34,287
Auto! Auto!

1008
01:01:35,068 --> 01:01:35,620
Auto!

1009
01:01:38,328 --> 01:01:38,912
Auto!

1010
01:01:46,778 --> 01:01:47,912
Do you know Bhaskar?

1011
01:01:48,495 --> 01:01:49,078
No, I don't know.

1012
01:01:51,329 --> 01:01:51,995
Hey!

1013
01:01:54,832 --> 01:01:57,120
Is Bhaskar here?

1014
01:01:59,296 --> 01:02:00,412
Do you know Bhaskar?

1015
01:02:00,766 --> 01:02:01,745
Tall guy.

1016
01:02:05,589 --> 01:02:06,507
Lord Govinda!

1017
01:02:13,674 --> 01:02:14,287
He is such a guy.

1018
01:02:15,479 --> 01:02:17,037
He loses anything I give him.

1019
01:02:17,933 --> 01:02:19,287
He cries as soon as he loses.

1020
01:02:19,787 --> 01:02:21,479
Where is my book, God?

1021
01:02:21,787 --> 01:02:24,474
My book is gone.

1022
01:02:24,701 --> 01:02:27,890
[Sanskrit]

1023
01:03:08,912 --> 01:03:09,870
What happened?

1024
01:03:10,912 --> 01:03:12,120
Looks like he lost some book.

1025
01:03:12,662 --> 01:03:13,662
Is it a cheque book?

1026
01:03:14,037 --> 01:03:15,495
We don't even
own a bank account.

1027
01:03:15,575 --> 01:03:17,287
-Then how would we have a cheque book?
-Exactly.

1028
01:03:19,162 --> 01:03:21,578
Hey, look. There are many
books in the school bag.

1029
01:03:21,870 --> 01:03:24,620
This is a notebook. This is
Mathematics. This is an English book.

1030
01:03:24,873 --> 01:03:26,841
There's even a Pedda
Bala Siksha book inside.

1031
01:03:27,703 --> 01:03:29,412
A book doesn't mean a
cheque book or a notebook.

1032
01:03:29,495 --> 01:03:30,537
Then what, a red book?

1033
01:03:30,765 --> 01:03:32,037
It's a God's gift book.

1034
01:03:33,457 --> 01:03:35,537
People like you won't
understand such books.

1035
01:03:36,245 --> 01:03:38,370
Only people like me, who have direct
contact with God, can understand it.

1036
01:03:38,592 --> 01:03:39,620
Such a useless book.

1037
01:03:39,965 --> 01:03:42,745
-We're suffering with of your stupidity.
-Hey, Venkata Ramana!

1038
01:03:42,995 --> 01:03:46,743
Forget admitting me in Apollo, first
get yourself treated in Erragadda.

1039
01:03:46,995 --> 01:03:48,412
You're the one who should be
admitted to Erragadda Hospital.

1040
01:03:49,662 --> 01:03:51,870
God speaks to me directly through Akashavani.

1041
01:03:52,245 --> 01:03:55,995
[cracking radio introduction]

1042
01:03:56,662 --> 01:03:58,453
Vijayawada Station.
News bulletin.

1043
01:03:58,787 --> 01:03:59,787
Is ended.

1044
01:04:00,745 --> 01:04:02,995
You won't believe me.
You won't listen to me.

1045
01:04:03,537 --> 01:04:04,578
Hey, Bhaskar.

1046
01:04:05,203 --> 01:04:06,203
Where had you gone?

1047
01:04:07,828 --> 01:04:09,495
Trouble comes knocking
at my door every single day.

1048
01:04:10,203 --> 01:04:12,662
-Why don't you knock on my door?
-Sir... sir.

1049
01:04:14,620 --> 01:04:15,620
I'm Bhaskar.

1050
01:04:15,953 --> 01:04:17,620
-Bhaskar!
-Yes, I'm Bhaskar.

1051
01:04:17,995 --> 01:04:18,995
Hey, book.

1052
01:04:19,370 --> 01:04:20,370
Hey, God!

1053
01:04:20,679 --> 01:04:22,453
You're there, my God.
I know you're there.

1054
01:04:22,703 --> 01:04:23,912
What happened, sir?
Why are you panicking?

1055
01:04:24,117 --> 01:04:25,412
-Bhaskar!
-Yes, I'm Bhaskar.

1056
01:04:25,495 --> 01:04:27,203
-Book!
-Yeah, you left it in the auto.

1057
01:04:28,037 --> 01:04:28,787
Oh, no!

1058
01:04:28,953 --> 01:04:31,537
Why are you so excited? It's not a cheque
book. It's just a normal book, right?

1059
01:04:32,037 --> 01:04:33,328
You're no ordinary man, Bhaskar.

1060
01:04:33,953 --> 01:04:36,537
You're just like Hanuman, who
delivered Sita's ring to Rama.

1061
01:04:36,870 --> 01:04:39,078
You're just like the little squirrel that
helped Lord Rama build Ram Setu.

1062
01:04:39,787 --> 01:04:40,912
You are my lucky Bhaskar.

1063
01:04:41,037 --> 01:04:42,328
Whether it's Lucky Bhaskar
or Bommarellu Bhaskar.

1064
01:04:42,453 --> 01:04:45,078
I came from Kukatpally just to return
this book to you. Give me Rs.100, sir.

1065
01:04:45,245 --> 01:04:46,412
Just Rs.100?

1066
01:04:46,870 --> 01:04:47,787
I'll give you Rs.10 lakhs.

1067
01:04:48,680 --> 01:04:50,037
No way. Make it Rs.50 lakhs.

1068
01:04:50,703 --> 01:04:52,328
Not Rs.50 lakhs, I'll
give you Rs.1 crore.

1069
01:04:54,703 --> 01:04:56,578
[all]: He's mad.

1070
01:04:58,578 --> 01:05:00,995
Not just mad, he's Mad Square.

1071
01:05:01,370 --> 01:05:03,870
I'll write my first wish in
the sacred Hour of Brahma.

1072
01:05:11,187 --> 01:05:13,966
[Sanskrit]

1073
01:05:29,468 --> 01:05:31,393
[Thunder rumbles]

1074
01:05:47,229 --> 01:05:48,991
[Thunder rumbles]

1075
01:05:55,870 --> 01:05:57,703
Pagadala Venkata Ramana.

1076
01:05:58,453 --> 01:06:01,662
Son of Pagadala Yedu Kondalu.

1077
01:06:04,995 --> 01:06:05,870
What amount should I write down?

1078
01:06:07,369 --> 01:06:08,078
I'll write down Rs.1 crore.

1079
01:06:11,120 --> 01:06:12,787
I think Rs.1 crore is too little.

1080
01:06:13,403 --> 01:06:14,412
Let me add a bit more.

1081
01:06:17,537 --> 01:06:18,995
The man who gave me this book is
Goddess Lakshmi's husband himself.

1082
01:06:19,693 --> 01:06:21,328
Lakshmi Devi might get
upset if I ask for too little.

1083
01:06:21,953 --> 01:06:22,953
Am I right, God?

1084
01:06:24,078 --> 01:06:25,287
Let me increase it some more.

1085
01:06:25,662 --> 01:06:27,495
I want Rs.100 crores.

1086
01:06:32,703 --> 01:06:34,495
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1087
01:06:35,370 --> 01:06:37,287
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1088
01:06:38,017 --> 01:06:39,828
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1089
01:06:40,370 --> 01:06:42,245
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1090
01:06:58,912 --> 01:07:00,495
Where exactly will
Rs.100 crores fall?

1091
01:07:02,030 --> 01:07:03,424
Is it going to fall
into my garden?

1092
01:07:03,738 --> 01:07:04,703
Let me see.

1093
01:07:04,783 --> 01:07:06,677
[Music]

1094
01:07:29,328 --> 01:07:31,328
Leave aside a hundred crores,
not even one rupee showed up.

1095
01:07:33,349 --> 01:07:34,745
God, why hasn't the
money shown up yet?

1096
01:07:36,495 --> 01:07:39,578
Maybe the Reserve Bank
doesn't have a hundred crores.

1097
01:07:41,238 --> 01:07:43,787
God, is asking for Rs.100
crores too ambitious?

1098
01:07:45,105 --> 01:07:48,620
Considering my status, I'll write
Rs.2 crores on the second page, God.

1099
01:07:48,856 --> 01:07:53,737
[Thunder rumbles]

1100
01:08:04,328 --> 01:08:05,662
What was that? Is it an earthquake?

1101
01:08:05,742 --> 01:08:07,703
There's no earthquake or
pineapple cake. Go to sleep.

1102
01:08:07,953 --> 01:08:08,787
I'll go and check.

1103
01:08:09,228 --> 01:08:10,190
Just sleep.

1104
01:08:23,662 --> 01:08:24,495
Oh God!

1105
01:08:30,037 --> 01:08:32,037
Oh Lord Venkateswara!

1106
01:08:33,586 --> 01:08:35,870
Oh God! The roof's broken open!

1107
01:08:36,328 --> 01:08:37,578
All these roof tiles...

1108
01:08:37,859 --> 01:08:38,912
Keep quiet, you idiot.

1109
01:08:39,245 --> 01:08:40,953
One hit with this hammer,
and your head will split open.

1110
01:08:42,745 --> 01:08:43,495
God!

1111
01:08:44,412 --> 01:08:46,120
Govinda… my Lord Govinda!

1112
01:09:06,795 --> 01:09:10,073
[Sanskrit]

1113
01:09:16,662 --> 01:09:19,287
I need to tell you
all an amazing truth.

1114
01:09:19,650 --> 01:09:20,370
What is it, dear?

1115
01:09:21,120 --> 01:09:23,412
Lord Venkateswara
requested Goddess Lakshmi…

1116
01:09:23,912 --> 01:09:25,912
and made all this
money fall into our house.

1117
01:09:26,340 --> 01:09:27,412
Is it?

1118
01:09:27,703 --> 01:09:29,245
But we don't believe it.

1119
01:09:30,995 --> 01:09:34,328
Some mafia don is passing
over our house in a helicopter…

1120
01:09:34,802 --> 01:09:36,912
and he dropped it due to overload.

1121
01:09:37,120 --> 01:09:38,328
This makes sense.

1122
01:09:38,912 --> 01:09:41,787
Whether it's the mafia don
or Lord Venkateshwara…

1123
01:09:42,287 --> 01:09:44,482
But in the end, we got a
huge amount of money.

1124
01:09:45,276 --> 01:09:48,328
With this money, let's get
a small tiled-roof house.

1125
01:09:49,370 --> 01:09:52,203
Why are you talking about a small house
when we have this huge money, you fool?

1126
01:09:54,037 --> 01:09:55,287
We'll buy a 5-bedroom villa!

1127
01:09:57,245 --> 01:09:58,662
The housewarming
ceremony will be held soon.

1128
01:10:20,037 --> 01:10:21,745
I got your problem.
Please wait for some time.

1129
01:10:22,202 --> 01:10:24,412
-Try to listen to me as well.
-Dear, have you seen outside?

1130
01:10:24,620 --> 01:10:25,620
It's a Mercedes Maybach.

1131
01:10:26,162 --> 01:10:27,745
They are buying a
Ferrari too, it seems.

1132
01:10:27,980 --> 01:10:31,537
We thought he would escape because
of loan problems. Will he buy a Ferrari?

1133
01:10:31,617 --> 01:10:32,328
-Yeah!
-Hmm!

1134
01:10:32,408 --> 01:10:33,960
Mr. Govardhan.

1135
01:10:34,328 --> 01:10:35,717
How's the house?

1136
01:10:36,620 --> 01:10:38,578
You can't even
manage food each day,

1137
01:10:39,078 --> 01:10:41,545
so how can you suddenly
afford this big villa?

1138
01:10:41,870 --> 01:10:43,370
I can digest even stones.

1139
01:10:43,828 --> 01:10:46,078
But I can't digest this
matter, Venkata Ramana.

1140
01:10:46,203 --> 01:10:47,620
-How is this possible?
-God's gift.

1141
01:10:47,846 --> 01:10:49,162
-The minister is here, brother-in-law.
-Yeah!

1142
01:10:49,789 --> 01:10:51,745
-Minister?
-That's how we should tell those fools.

1143
01:10:51,912 --> 01:10:53,995
-Your status has risen now.
-Correct.

1144
01:11:02,078 --> 01:11:04,287
Venkata Ramana is only meant
to decorate the house with flowers.

1145
01:11:04,578 --> 01:11:06,453
But how did he get this house
with all this flower decoration?

1146
01:11:06,533 --> 01:11:08,453
Leave him, think
about his father.

1147
01:11:08,674 --> 01:11:13,412
His father seems like someone
who buys old used clothes.

1148
01:11:13,725 --> 01:11:15,787
How is he worthy of
silk clothes, brother?

1149
01:11:17,495 --> 01:11:20,620
This family doesn't deserve
even a clean bathroom in this villa.

1150
01:11:21,620 --> 01:11:23,832
Calling them millionaires is an
insult to the entire class of millionaires.

1151
01:11:23,912 --> 01:11:25,037
-Let's go.
-She said right?

1152
01:11:27,287 --> 01:11:31,287
To destroy them, I will bring Aghoras
from Kashi and perform a dark ritual.

1153
01:11:31,765 --> 01:11:34,703
We must not stop our protest
until they have lost everything.

1154
01:11:34,870 --> 01:11:36,370
We will spend as much
as necessary for that.

1155
01:11:36,597 --> 01:11:37,703
Ready!

1156
01:11:39,287 --> 01:11:41,995
Dear, will everything they
say actually come true?

1157
01:11:42,495 --> 01:11:44,078
It is not what they said...

1158
01:11:44,703 --> 01:11:46,245
what I have written
will come true.

1159
01:12:07,120 --> 01:12:13,083
Panjagutta S.I. Gundla Ramakrishna,
who has a bad mindset toward women,

1160
01:12:13,573 --> 01:12:15,078
should lose what he loves most.

1161
01:12:15,482 --> 01:12:17,162
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1162
01:12:50,328 --> 01:12:52,453
Oh my God! What's gone wrong?

1163
01:12:55,828 --> 01:12:57,828
It's not even in the
commode. Oh my God!

1164
01:12:58,245 --> 01:12:59,745
How did I miss that part?

1165
01:13:00,453 --> 01:13:03,573
Where has it gone? It should be
in the blanket, right? Where is it?

1166
01:13:04,215 --> 01:13:06,328
-Why is it not finding?
-What are you searching for?

1167
01:13:06,620 --> 01:13:09,469
-I missed something important.
-Important matter?

1168
01:13:09,689 --> 01:13:11,120
Should I place an
order on Swiggy?

1169
01:13:11,370 --> 01:13:14,370
You're not able to order
it on Swiggy or Zomato.

1170
01:13:14,450 --> 01:13:17,071
-Then?
-It is a very important matter.

1171
01:13:17,151 --> 01:13:19,120
What is that so important thing for you?

1172
01:13:19,287 --> 01:13:20,287
It's not for me…

1173
01:13:20,367 --> 01:13:22,620
It's something important
for you, Susheela.

1174
01:13:22,700 --> 01:13:24,203
-It's important for you, Susheela.
-For me?

1175
01:13:24,287 --> 01:13:26,370
Doctor! Doctor!

1176
01:13:26,620 --> 01:13:27,662
-Doctor!
-Hey!

1177
01:13:27,912 --> 01:13:31,915
I saw a patient walk in wearing
shorts, pants, and a lungi.

1178
01:13:31,995 --> 01:13:34,957
-Why did you come wearing just a towel?
-I missed it, doctor.

1179
01:13:35,037 --> 01:13:36,037
What exactly did you miss?

1180
01:13:38,203 --> 01:13:39,162
I missed it, doctor.

1181
01:13:40,078 --> 01:13:42,078
-Write it down, he missed it.
-Don't write it, dear.

1182
01:13:43,203 --> 01:13:45,037
I like it a lot, doctor.

1183
01:13:45,328 --> 01:13:48,162
Everything is important for a human being.
I'm asking you what exactly you missed.

1184
01:13:48,370 --> 01:13:49,245
Well, that is…

1185
01:13:51,075 --> 01:13:52,537
It's like an injection for doctors.

1186
01:13:52,995 --> 01:13:54,162
Like a gear for a car.

1187
01:13:54,870 --> 01:13:56,078
Like a baton for the police.

1188
01:13:56,662 --> 01:13:59,078
I missed such an item
in my body, doctor.

1189
01:13:59,370 --> 01:14:00,370
Oh shit!

1190
01:14:00,870 --> 01:14:03,412
-You mean this part?
-Exactly.

1191
01:14:03,787 --> 01:14:05,120
-I won't believe you.
-You won't believe?

1192
01:14:05,328 --> 01:14:06,537
-I said I can't believe it.
-Then see it yourself.

1193
01:14:07,745 --> 01:14:09,787
-Madam, could you step out for a while?
-No.

1194
01:14:10,328 --> 01:14:12,412
I will listen to all problems.
I will look into every problem.

1195
01:14:12,662 --> 01:14:14,162
-I've seen my doctors as well.
-Hey! Hey!

1196
01:14:14,757 --> 01:14:17,162
-I meant X-ray!
-[both]: Oh, you mean X-ray.

1197
01:14:17,537 --> 01:14:18,662
Then take a look!

1198
01:14:19,953 --> 01:14:22,412
What is this? I've never seen it before.

1199
01:14:22,828 --> 01:14:25,412
-Okay, okay. No problem.
-Doctor!

1200
01:14:25,537 --> 01:14:26,995
Cool!
-Two doctors are in danger here.

1201
01:14:27,287 --> 01:14:29,662
-Come fast.
-Stop it!

1202
01:14:29,742 --> 01:14:30,832
-Sit there.
-Have a seat!

1203
01:14:30,912 --> 01:14:32,870
-She said she has seen many cases?
-You just sit there, man.

1204
01:14:34,066 --> 01:14:35,370
What about my situation, doctor?

1205
01:14:36,076 --> 01:14:37,377
[Calling bell rings]

1206
01:14:37,766 --> 01:14:40,328
Since the playground is empty,
all the matches are cancelled.

1207
01:14:40,453 --> 01:14:41,453
Oh God!

1208
01:14:41,828 --> 01:14:43,154
Gods must be crazy.

1209
01:14:46,010 --> 01:14:49,412
Two lakhs, three lakhs, four lakhs, five
lakhs, seven lakhs…

1210
01:14:49,658 --> 01:14:51,415
Why are you transferring so much money?

1211
01:14:51,495 --> 01:14:52,985
-Is this for a new business?
-Yes, dear.

1212
01:14:53,328 --> 01:14:54,620
It's a charitable business.

1213
01:14:54,870 --> 01:14:57,665
-What kind of business is that?
-I have started a new business.

1214
01:14:58,578 --> 01:15:03,248
I've sent 5 lakhs to every family
affected by the bus accident in Chevella.

1215
01:15:03,328 --> 01:15:07,839
I have sent 10 lakhs to each house of a
devotee who died in Tukkisalat in Kasibugga

1216
01:15:07,919 --> 01:15:09,957
God! What has happened to you?

1217
01:15:10,037 --> 01:15:14,248
Are you a Telangana CM or Andhra CM to
help those families?

1218
01:15:14,328 --> 01:15:15,328
You stupid!

1219
01:15:15,578 --> 01:15:17,276
I don't know what the reason is.

1220
01:15:17,745 --> 01:15:19,412
My heart is drawn towards charity.

1221
01:15:19,620 --> 01:15:21,662
-Sir!
-Good riddance if you drop dead as well.

1222
01:15:28,088 --> 01:15:28,953
Salary, sir.

1223
01:15:29,625 --> 01:15:31,287
-How much?
-5,000 rupees.

1224
01:15:33,376 --> 01:15:34,912
5,000 rupees is not enough for you.

1225
01:15:35,217 --> 01:15:36,162
How will you survive?

1226
01:15:36,805 --> 01:15:37,453
See!

1227
01:15:38,021 --> 01:15:41,537
There are 5 lakhs in this.
Take it.

1228
01:15:42,159 --> 01:15:44,453
-Thank you, sir.
-What is this mess? Get out.

1229
01:15:45,328 --> 01:15:46,230
-Just go, she is like that only.
-Get out.

1230
01:15:46,449 --> 01:15:47,885
[Cell phone rings]

1231
01:15:48,561 --> 01:15:49,828
It would have been better
if you had been hit by the gravel...

1232
01:15:50,037 --> 01:15:51,601
-from that tipper truck accident.
-Hello, Is it an orphanage?

1233
01:15:52,057 --> 01:15:53,578
-Hey, where are you going?
-Tell me how many crores you want.

1234
01:16:01,078 --> 01:16:01,828
It's unfair.

1235
01:16:02,162 --> 01:16:03,037
-What, Bhaskar!
-Sir!

1236
01:16:03,117 --> 01:16:04,412
Why didn't you come when I invited
you for the housewarming ceremony?

1237
01:16:04,995 --> 01:16:05,995
It's just my bad luck, sir.

1238
01:16:06,484 --> 01:16:09,120
Yesterday a passenger left a vegetables
bag in the auto.

1239
01:16:09,370 --> 01:16:10,328
They are green sorrel leaves.

1240
01:16:10,745 --> 01:16:15,370
I thought I would make mutton curry,
but the police came and arrested me.

1241
01:16:15,450 --> 01:16:17,495
-For what?
-It's not sorrel leaves, it's weed.

1242
01:16:17,784 --> 01:16:19,537
-Bad luck.
-That's what I told you earlier.

1243
01:16:21,662 --> 01:16:23,203
-What is this, sir?
-Luck.

1244
01:16:26,745 --> 01:16:28,120
One crore rupees
that I promise you.

1245
01:16:28,494 --> 01:16:29,370
One crore rupees?

1246
01:16:29,662 --> 01:16:32,120
You are not bad luck,
Bhaskar anymore. You are lucky, Bhaskar.

1247
01:16:32,870 --> 01:16:34,662
I thought you had gone mad that day.

1248
01:16:34,995 --> 01:16:36,037
But you are really great, sir.

1249
01:16:36,953 --> 01:16:38,453
-You are like God to me, sir.
-Hey, Bhaskar.

1250
01:16:39,203 --> 01:16:40,162
Thank you, sir.

1251
01:16:40,639 --> 01:16:41,620
-Thank you.
-Bye.

1252
01:16:49,370 --> 01:16:50,453
Dude, I'm nearby.

1253
01:16:50,620 --> 01:16:52,162
Yeah, I'm on the way. Just wait.

1254
01:16:56,620 --> 01:16:58,453
[heavy panting]

1255
01:17:05,953 --> 01:17:08,537
-Do you think he'll survive, dear?
-It's difficult, Grandma. He won't survive.

1256
01:17:08,870 --> 01:17:10,787
God has no mercy, dear.

1257
01:17:16,536 --> 01:17:20,556
[Sanskrit]

1258
01:17:37,245 --> 01:17:39,880
Brother, check the ID card and
tell me his name and address.

1259
01:17:59,356 --> 01:18:01,620
-His name is Rakesh.
-Rakesh.

1260
01:18:05,708 --> 01:18:07,995
Sales Executive at Blue
J Real Estate Company.

1261
01:18:08,275 --> 01:18:09,662
Blue J Real Estate Company.

1262
01:18:10,032 --> 01:18:12,414
That boy must not die.

1263
01:18:20,285 --> 01:18:23,245
Om namo Venkateshaya.

1264
01:18:53,703 --> 01:18:54,703
Hey, wait. I'm coming.

1265
01:18:56,745 --> 01:18:57,912
I'm Lord Yama.

1266
01:18:58,828 --> 01:19:00,495
What force dared to stop me?

1267
01:19:00,758 --> 01:19:04,998
[Sanskrit]

1268
01:19:18,912 --> 01:19:20,120
You're Lord Yama, aren't you?

1269
01:19:20,828 --> 01:19:21,828
Are you able to see me?

1270
01:19:22,328 --> 01:19:23,703
I can see and hear you clearly.

1271
01:19:24,245 --> 01:19:28,703
But the Lord Yama I know
is... actor NTR, Kaikala Satyanarayana...

1272
01:19:29,037 --> 01:19:32,495
Dr. M Mohan Babu... young Tiger
NTR for the current generation.

1273
01:19:33,370 --> 01:19:36,162
Why do you look as
thin as a thermometer?

1274
01:19:36,912 --> 01:19:39,745
That's because I got diabetes
from constantly carrying the mace.

1275
01:19:39,912 --> 01:19:41,495
Even Lord Yama got diabetes?

1276
01:19:43,203 --> 01:19:44,495
Leave you aside, Lord.

1277
01:19:44,953 --> 01:19:47,120
Why is your bull even skinnier than you?

1278
01:19:47,620 --> 01:19:49,037
It's suffering from low sugar.

1279
01:19:49,412 --> 01:19:54,796
It's been carrying Lord Yama for
ages, so it lost some muscle mass.

1280
01:19:55,453 --> 01:19:57,953
No matter who comes into this
world, sugar is common for everyone.

1281
01:19:58,370 --> 01:20:01,912
He's not even 25 years old. How
could you decide to take his life, sir?

1282
01:20:02,203 --> 01:20:03,787
-Sir?
-Yes!

1283
01:20:04,745 --> 01:20:07,078
It is Lord Brahma who decides
the birth and death of people.

1284
01:20:07,287 --> 01:20:09,537
My duty is to carry it out.

1285
01:20:10,323 --> 01:20:12,787
This was his first mortal peril,
so he managed to escape it.

1286
01:20:13,162 --> 01:20:16,828
Next time, I'll definitely take
his life with this noose of Yama.

1287
01:20:17,037 --> 01:20:19,412
-His death is inevitable.
-Lord!

1288
01:20:19,662 --> 01:20:23,287
[voice echoing]

1289
01:20:25,995 --> 01:20:27,078
Tell me, Venkata Ramana.

1290
01:20:27,495 --> 01:20:29,328
A lean Yama is standing next to me.

1291
01:20:29,453 --> 01:20:30,328
A lean Yama?

1292
01:20:30,745 --> 01:20:34,412
There aren't different Yamas
like skinny Yama and giant Yama.

1293
01:20:34,870 --> 01:20:36,370
There's only one Lord Yama.

1294
01:20:37,037 --> 01:20:37,995
Tell me what the matter is.

1295
01:20:38,453 --> 01:20:39,787
He says he's
going to take his life.

1296
01:20:39,995 --> 01:20:41,203
This is a challenge
to my self-respect.

1297
01:20:41,412 --> 01:20:43,037
Will the things written in the
book you gave me come true?

1298
01:20:43,328 --> 01:20:44,495
Or will Yama's words come true?

1299
01:20:44,828 --> 01:20:47,120
Once you write it in that book,

1300
01:20:47,995 --> 01:20:52,287
even Lord Brahma, who
writes fate, cannot change it.

1301
01:20:52,662 --> 01:20:54,537
What kind of writing is this?
You've got four heads.

1302
01:20:54,787 --> 01:20:56,245
You haven't written
even one fate properly.

1303
01:20:58,203 --> 01:21:00,120
Venkata Ramana!

1304
01:21:00,453 --> 01:21:01,828
Oh! Seems like the Lord got offended.

1305
01:21:02,120 --> 01:21:03,787
Forgive me, Lord.
I'll speak with you later.

1306
01:21:05,162 --> 01:21:07,412
I declare this before the five
natural elements as my witness.

1307
01:21:08,037 --> 01:21:10,662
You're ridiculing God using
the blessings He gave you.

1308
01:21:11,120 --> 01:21:13,578
Altering the destiny
written by the Creator...

1309
01:21:14,037 --> 01:21:15,870
will warp the very
laws of deeds.

1310
01:21:16,203 --> 01:21:20,537
The consequences of past,
present, and future deeds...

1311
01:21:20,870 --> 01:21:25,120
...the sins of past lives, the ancestral
curses, and the wrath of deities...

1312
01:21:25,495 --> 01:21:27,412
humans must endure them all.

1313
01:21:27,828 --> 01:21:28,620
Oh!

1314
01:21:29,120 --> 01:21:32,453
Garikapati and Chaganti preach
these same things every day.

1315
01:21:32,620 --> 01:21:36,203
If I report you to the Blue Cross
for harassing a bull all these years,

1316
01:21:36,662 --> 01:21:40,494
you won't even be
allowed to stay on this earth.

1317
01:21:51,662 --> 01:21:54,287
I must make Padma
understand about this book.

1318
01:21:56,912 --> 01:21:57,662
Yeah.

1319
01:21:57,995 --> 01:22:00,207
-Padma, I need to tell you something.
-Just wait a moment.

1320
01:22:00,287 --> 01:22:02,162
-Let the kids finish their homework.
-[Both]: Venkata Ramana!

1321
01:22:02,662 --> 01:22:03,412
Oh!

1322
01:22:08,370 --> 01:22:12,537
From the day of your housewarming,
our house has been filled with bad luck.

1323
01:22:13,287 --> 01:22:15,703
My husband keeps visiting
doctors wearing only a towel,

1324
01:22:15,787 --> 01:22:18,427
claiming he
lost something important.

1325
01:22:21,537 --> 01:22:27,245
He is feeling incredibly sad
while watching the movie Uppena.

1326
01:22:27,995 --> 01:22:32,287
Because of him, my son and I
are left begging on the streets.

1327
01:22:32,995 --> 01:22:36,120
Please do something and bring
them back to normal, Venkata Ramana.

1328
01:22:36,537 --> 01:22:39,037
-I will take care of it. Don't worry.
-Don't forget, Venkata Ramana.

1329
01:22:39,287 --> 01:22:40,203
I definitely won't forget.

1330
01:22:42,287 --> 01:22:43,828
Padma, let's go to a restaurant.

1331
01:22:44,078 --> 01:22:45,078
Let's talk there.

1332
01:22:46,995 --> 01:22:47,620
Sir!

1333
01:22:47,912 --> 01:22:48,912
-Bring two fruit punches.
-Yes, sir.

1334
01:22:50,745 --> 01:22:51,703
-Padma!
-Hmm!

1335
01:22:51,953 --> 01:22:53,412
You must believe
what I'm going to say.

1336
01:22:53,912 --> 01:22:56,453
-The reason we earn money is...
-It's because of Lord Venkateswara, right?

1337
01:22:56,620 --> 01:22:57,495
Hey! That's right.

1338
01:22:59,536 --> 01:23:00,370
Won't you ever change?

1339
01:23:02,453 --> 01:23:03,203
She is not believing it.

1340
01:23:03,537 --> 01:23:04,745
How do I make her believe it?

1341
01:23:20,078 --> 01:23:21,120
-Hey, come on!
-Hey, Rakesh!

1342
01:23:21,328 --> 01:23:22,245
-Hey, Rakesh!
-What are you doing?

1343
01:23:22,412 --> 01:23:23,162
-Leave me.
-Leave her.

1344
01:23:23,328 --> 01:23:24,412
Padma, I'll be back shortly.

1345
01:23:24,745 --> 01:23:25,412
Dear!

1346
01:23:25,914 --> 01:23:27,703
-Rakesh, leave me. Leave me.
-Hey!

1347
01:23:28,370 --> 01:23:29,370
-Hey!
-Rakesh!

1348
01:23:29,662 --> 01:23:31,037
-I am telling you.
-Leave me.

1349
01:23:31,412 --> 01:23:33,203
-Leave her. Manasa!
-Hey! Come on!

1350
01:23:34,203 --> 01:23:35,370
-Rakesh, leave me.
-Rakesh

1351
01:23:38,703 --> 01:23:40,203
Rakesh, what are you doing?

1352
01:23:40,620 --> 01:23:41,370
Leave her.

1353
01:23:41,745 --> 01:23:43,370
-Manasa! Manasa!
-Hey!

1354
01:23:44,037 --> 01:23:44,912
Hey!

1355
01:23:45,370 --> 01:23:46,620
-Hey!
-Manasa!

1356
01:23:47,495 --> 01:23:49,412
Someone please help!

1357
01:23:49,703 --> 01:23:51,995
-Dear!
-Manasa! Manasa!

1358
01:23:52,995 --> 01:23:55,662
-What happened?
-Let's go to the hospital. You'll be fine.

1359
01:23:55,912 --> 01:23:57,203
She's bleeding heavily.

1360
01:23:59,203 --> 01:24:00,037
Oh no!

1361
01:24:00,328 --> 01:24:01,703
-Please hurry up.
-Where has the book gone?

1362
01:24:04,370 --> 01:24:06,453
Padma, take her to
the hospital immediately.

1363
01:24:06,703 --> 01:24:08,162
-I will join there.
-Okay, dear.

1364
01:24:08,828 --> 01:24:09,745
Don't delay.

1365
01:24:10,620 --> 01:24:11,828
You scored just seven marks.

1366
01:24:12,287 --> 01:24:13,287
What is this, Arjun?

1367
01:24:13,578 --> 01:24:14,453
Show me your hand.

1368
01:24:14,912 --> 01:24:17,120
No, ma'am. Please, ma'am, no.

1369
01:24:18,620 --> 01:24:23,203
If you score low marks, the teacher
will also beat you with a scale.

1370
01:24:44,277 --> 01:24:48,370
Alphores School,
Hyderabad, Fifth-grade student...

1371
01:24:49,006 --> 01:24:53,162
Balaji, son of Venkata
Ramana, should score 79 marks.

1372
01:24:53,328 --> 01:24:55,245
Om namo Venkateshaya!

1373
01:25:02,703 --> 01:25:03,828
-Balaji!
-Yes, ma'am.

1374
01:25:04,078 --> 01:25:05,078
Come here!

1375
01:25:09,537 --> 01:25:12,328
Last time you got only 7
marks. Now you got 79 marks.

1376
01:25:12,703 --> 01:25:14,641
Everyone, clap for him.
- [Claps]

1377
01:25:16,495 --> 01:25:18,453
Balaji, you are
very hardworking.

1378
01:25:18,745 --> 01:25:20,537
It's not hard work or nothing.

1379
01:25:20,745 --> 01:25:22,203
I got these marks
because I wrote in this book.

1380
01:25:22,412 --> 01:25:24,328
What do you mean by that?

1381
01:25:29,831 --> 01:25:30,537
Hey!

1382
01:25:30,995 --> 01:25:32,287
How did you get high marks?

1383
01:25:32,912 --> 01:25:35,703
Did you copy, or
did you hide slips?

1384
01:25:37,162 --> 01:25:39,537
-Hey, he copied.
-Yes.

1385
01:25:45,328 --> 01:25:46,643
Make arrangements
for the operation.

1386
01:25:50,537 --> 01:25:54,078
G.Praveen, studying in 5th class,

1387
01:25:54,412 --> 01:25:56,662
C-Section, Roll Number
18, in Alphores School.

1388
01:25:57,037 --> 01:26:00,578
He should bang his head on the
wall and injure his nose so it bleeds.

1389
01:26:00,995 --> 01:26:02,578
Om namo Venkateshaya.

1390
01:26:08,620 --> 01:26:09,620
-Yes!
-Yes!

1391
01:26:18,953 --> 01:26:23,120
-Hey! How dare you laugh at me?
-Hey, no. Stop.

1392
01:26:23,537 --> 01:26:27,245
He has a powerful book. Whatever
he writes in that book will come true.

1393
01:26:27,412 --> 01:26:28,662
Don't mess with him.

1394
01:26:34,578 --> 01:26:35,578
Daddy!

1395
01:26:36,537 --> 01:26:37,537
Hey!

1396
01:26:38,870 --> 01:26:39,787
Give me that book.

1397
01:26:45,120 --> 01:26:47,162
-Yes, tell me.
-The girl's name is Manasa.

1398
01:26:47,360 --> 01:26:50,927
[Sanskrit]

1399
01:26:52,453 --> 01:26:53,995
[muted voice]

1400
01:27:02,078 --> 01:27:03,828
[muted voice]

1401
01:27:29,578 --> 01:27:31,287
[In Sanskit]: You are
entitled to perform your duty,

1402
01:27:31,620 --> 01:27:33,037
but never to the
outcome of your actions.

1403
01:27:33,828 --> 01:27:35,537
You should never involve
yourself as the cause of the results,

1404
01:27:35,995 --> 01:27:37,870
and at the same time never
remain idle without doing your duty.

1405
01:27:38,328 --> 01:27:41,162
You have the right to
perform your duties alone...

1406
01:27:41,703 --> 01:27:42,828
but never over their results.

1407
01:27:43,203 --> 01:27:45,578
You should never involve
yourself as the cause of the results,

1408
01:27:45,953 --> 01:27:48,578
and at the same time never
remain idle without doing your duty.

1409
01:27:49,870 --> 01:27:52,870
You have rewritten destiny itself
and written a completely new fate.

1410
01:27:53,370 --> 01:27:56,703
As a result, a wicked man who
should have died has survived.

1411
01:27:59,995 --> 01:28:02,745
A girl who was supposed to
become a doctor lost her life.

1412
01:28:07,287 --> 01:28:10,995
What you see isn't always good,
and what you can't see isn't always bad.

1413
01:28:11,287 --> 01:28:13,203
What you wrote is not
considered destiny at all.

1414
01:28:14,120 --> 01:28:17,745
Lord Brahma writes the ultimate
retribution for every sin a human commits.

1415
01:28:19,912 --> 01:28:23,370
Karma will hunt you
down for altering that fate.

1416
01:28:23,620 --> 01:28:26,453
[voice echoing]

1417
01:28:37,287 --> 01:28:38,120
Daddy!
Daddy!

1418
01:28:38,495 --> 01:28:41,037
-Why is your nose bleeding?
-Forget about my nose, there's a book.

1419
01:28:41,287 --> 01:28:41,953
A book?

1420
01:28:42,120 --> 01:28:46,995
Venkat Ramana, who once worked in our
hotel, became rich because of this book.

1421
01:28:47,162 --> 01:28:50,078
Whatever he writes in that
book will come true, Dad.

1422
01:28:50,495 --> 01:28:51,495
What kind of book is that?

1423
01:28:57,472 --> 01:28:58,870
-You're naughty!
-Hello!

1424
01:28:59,120 --> 01:29:01,453
-Who is this?
-We are from the Income Tax Department.

1425
01:29:02,453 --> 01:29:04,120
Since you are an Income Tax Officer,

1426
01:29:04,412 --> 01:29:07,953
you should raid Venkat Ramana's
house and get us all the books from there.

1427
01:29:09,328 --> 01:29:11,245
We got information
that half of the money...

1428
01:29:11,483 --> 01:29:13,162
that should be in the
World Bank is with you.

1429
01:29:13,995 --> 01:29:15,495
Come on!
Search!

1430
01:29:15,699 --> 01:29:17,953
Hey, damn. Stop it!

1431
01:29:18,953 --> 01:29:20,328
I don't mean search me.

1432
01:29:20,787 --> 01:29:23,495
Search the whole house. Go and search. Go!

1433
01:29:24,453 --> 01:29:25,912
No one should go out.

1434
01:29:26,203 --> 01:29:26,953
Close the doors.

1435
01:29:27,120 --> 01:29:28,662
Okay, sir.
Let's go.

1436
01:29:29,287 --> 01:29:30,453
This looks like a
rich man's house.

1437
01:29:30,703 --> 01:29:31,370
Hey!

1438
01:29:31,578 --> 01:29:32,328
Hey!

1439
01:29:32,620 --> 01:29:33,953
Hey!

1440
01:29:34,870 --> 01:29:35,787
What are you doing?

1441
01:29:35,912 --> 01:29:37,794
Didn't you ask me to
go in and shut the door?

1442
01:29:38,537 --> 01:29:41,245
I meant close the main door.

1443
01:29:41,537 --> 01:29:45,245
That doesn't mean you take the
maid into the kitchen and lock the door.

1444
01:29:45,482 --> 01:29:47,537
-Bobby!
-Hey! How disgusting.

1445
01:29:53,662 --> 01:29:55,787
Oh my God!

1446
01:29:56,120 --> 01:29:59,120
This house doesn't
seem built with bricks.

1447
01:29:59,537 --> 01:30:02,537
It looks like it's
made of money bags.

1448
01:30:02,787 --> 01:30:04,287
Hello! What business
do you have in my house?

1449
01:30:04,537 --> 01:30:06,870
This is too much. Speak to them only
after my brother and sister-in-law comes.

1450
01:30:07,739 --> 01:30:09,870
There she comes,
the pointing girl.

1451
01:30:10,753 --> 01:30:12,495
-Where are your brother and sister-in-law?
-Sir!

1452
01:30:13,162 --> 01:30:14,662
This is the single
plot, total 40 acres.

1453
01:30:15,078 --> 01:30:16,953
-They're quoting 70 crores.
-It doesn't matter what the cost is.

1454
01:30:17,287 --> 01:30:19,037
-Let's speak to the owner first.
-Okay, sir.

1455
01:30:23,703 --> 01:30:26,453
Most importantly, there's a book called
"God's Gift." Don't miss it at any cost.

1456
01:30:26,953 --> 01:30:32,253
Everything is here… but I
couldn't find that "God's Gift" book.

1457
01:30:35,537 --> 01:30:36,828
Sir, we searched everywhere
in the house,

1458
01:30:37,037 --> 01:30:38,912
but we couldn't find the God's
Gift book you mentioned.

1459
01:30:39,662 --> 01:30:40,578
I see.

1460
01:30:44,347 --> 01:30:47,401
[Sanskrit]

1461
01:31:01,828 --> 01:31:03,078
Padma, let's go.

1462
01:31:25,995 --> 01:31:29,657
I will bring the God's Gift
book and give it to you as a gift.

1463
01:31:34,967 --> 01:31:38,224
[Police siren wails]

1464
01:31:43,078 --> 01:31:43,828
There he is.

1465
01:31:44,120 --> 01:31:45,120
He is here.

1466
01:31:45,412 --> 01:31:46,370
Are you here, brother-in-law?

1467
01:31:46,578 --> 01:31:48,370
Sir, did you find the book?

1468
01:31:48,662 --> 01:31:51,245
I think this book is
very important to him.

1469
01:31:51,537 --> 01:31:53,953
He placed it under the feet
of Lord Venkateswara's idol.

1470
01:31:54,453 --> 01:31:55,287
Thanks, brother-in-law.

1471
01:31:55,578 --> 01:31:59,328
-Love you, brother-in-law.
-Oh, sorry. I love only Silk Smitha.

1472
01:31:59,662 --> 01:32:02,022
-Bye.
-[both]: Bye! Bye!

1473
01:32:02,287 --> 01:32:03,078
Bye, brother-in-law.

1474
01:32:03,412 --> 01:32:04,162
Get in.

1475
01:32:05,995 --> 01:32:07,620
Brother-in-law, we
finally found the book.

1476
01:32:08,662 --> 01:32:12,245
Let's write about recovering my lost part
and your property. Come on, write it down.

1477
01:32:12,412 --> 01:32:13,953
-It's a wrong decision, brother-in-law.
-Why?

1478
01:32:14,203 --> 01:32:15,620
It's fine even if we
don't become rich,

1479
01:32:15,995 --> 01:32:17,578
but Venkata Ramana
should be ruined completely.

1480
01:32:17,787 --> 01:32:21,037
He should end up washing
cups in my hotel… he should cry.

1481
01:32:21,245 --> 01:32:22,745
-I'll write that.
-Okay, write it.

1482
01:32:23,578 --> 01:32:27,412
Venkata Ramana should lose all
his property and end up on the streets.

1483
01:32:27,620 --> 01:32:29,953
He should beg.
Om Namo Vekateshaya.

1484
01:32:31,745 --> 01:32:33,870
Count the 40 crores that
Venkata Ramana gave.

1485
01:32:33,995 --> 01:32:34,745
Okay, sir.

1486
01:32:48,120 --> 01:32:50,360
Sir, there are only
white papers here.

1487
01:32:51,287 --> 01:32:52,120
White papers?

1488
01:33:12,912 --> 01:33:14,162
Sir, this is the
villa that I sold.

1489
01:33:14,703 --> 01:33:16,745
-Why are you so tense?
-You won't understand even if I tell you.

1490
01:33:16,825 --> 01:33:17,953
I will take care of it.

1491
01:33:18,203 --> 01:33:20,537
Don't you have any shame cheating
while taking God's name as your identity?

1492
01:33:20,953 --> 01:33:21,703
What did I do?

1493
01:33:21,912 --> 01:33:24,021
-You gave me only white papers.
-White papers?

1494
01:33:24,370 --> 01:33:25,662
Yes.
Stop.

1495
01:33:25,912 --> 01:33:27,620
You'll understand everything at
the police station. Take him, sir.

1496
01:33:27,787 --> 01:33:29,578
-Let's go to the station. Come on.
-Please listen to me, sir.

1497
01:33:29,913 --> 01:33:31,453
-Listen to me, sir.
-White papers?

1498
01:33:32,078 --> 01:33:33,078
Venkata Ramana.

1499
01:33:35,912 --> 01:33:36,745
What happened, dear?

1500
01:33:36,912 --> 01:33:38,703
He may have lost all his property
by now. Now write about us.

1501
01:33:39,037 --> 01:33:40,787
Everything is happening
just as it is written in the book.

1502
01:33:41,037 --> 01:33:42,037
Now see...

1503
01:33:42,117 --> 01:33:43,332
[Gunshot]

1504
01:33:43,412 --> 01:33:45,703
-Oh my God!
-Oh no!

1505
01:33:49,912 --> 01:33:51,203
My name is Muniswamy.

1506
01:33:52,162 --> 01:33:54,495
Each person does some job to survive.

1507
01:33:55,078 --> 01:33:57,745
But I steal cars to survive.

1508
01:33:58,078 --> 01:33:59,412
-Why is he coming here?
-Hey! Get down.

1509
01:33:59,703 --> 01:34:01,370
-Who the hell are you?
-What?

1510
01:34:01,578 --> 01:34:04,495
Won't you step down until I show
my Aadhaar card and voter list?

1511
01:34:04,620 --> 01:34:05,245
I mean...

1512
01:34:05,370 --> 01:34:06,328
-Just get down.
-Yes, I'm getting down.

1513
01:34:06,662 --> 01:34:08,203
-Get down.
-I'm getting down. I got down.

1514
01:34:10,745 --> 01:34:11,328
Hey!

1515
01:34:11,662 --> 01:34:13,453
-You bloody thief!
-Brother-in-law, he's stealing our car!

1516
01:34:13,703 --> 01:34:14,828
It's okay. It's just a
useless car anyway.

1517
01:34:15,245 --> 01:34:17,870
Write in the book that two
Range Rovers are for both of us.

1518
01:34:18,037 --> 01:34:19,828
I can write it, but
the book is in the car.

1519
01:34:23,537 --> 01:34:24,537
Susheela.

1520
01:34:24,703 --> 01:34:26,245
Brother-in-law, my car has navigation.

1521
01:34:26,453 --> 01:34:27,620
[both]: Auto, please stop.

1522
01:34:27,787 --> 01:34:28,495
Brother-in-law, get in.

1523
01:34:28,703 --> 01:34:30,703
I'll show you the route.
Follow that vehicle.

1524
01:34:31,245 --> 01:34:31,870
Get down.

1525
01:34:32,120 --> 01:34:33,370
-Why?
-Get down.

1526
01:34:34,703 --> 01:34:36,245
How can you speak like
that without any respect?

1527
01:34:36,495 --> 01:34:38,412
Your face gives a
very bad-luck vibe.

1528
01:34:39,370 --> 01:34:41,662
I don't respect unlucky
people, and I don't give lifts too.

1529
01:34:42,078 --> 01:34:43,078
I have to wash the
seat with phenyl.

1530
01:34:43,245 --> 01:34:44,245
-Get lost, you idiot. -Hey!

1531
01:34:45,412 --> 01:34:47,120
Brother-in-law, the
navigation stopped working.

1532
01:34:47,370 --> 01:34:48,287
Then what he said is correct.

1533
01:34:48,495 --> 01:34:49,787
-What did he say?
-He said we are unlucky people.

1534
01:34:49,912 --> 01:34:51,453
How does he know
we are unlucky people?

1535
01:34:51,578 --> 01:34:52,578
[both]: How?

1536
01:34:54,662 --> 01:34:55,453
Come inside.

1537
01:34:55,828 --> 01:34:56,870
Consider this your own house.

1538
01:34:57,078 --> 01:34:57,953
-Greetings.
-Greetings.

1539
01:34:58,370 --> 01:35:00,037
-Give coffee to everyone.
-Why is this happening, priest?

1540
01:35:00,703 --> 01:35:02,828
God is playing with our lives.

1541
01:35:08,482 --> 01:35:09,412
Sit down, dear.

1542
01:35:11,537 --> 01:35:12,537
Don't worry, dear.

1543
01:35:13,037 --> 01:35:14,537
God will take care of everything.

1544
01:35:15,620 --> 01:35:16,870
There is no God.

1545
01:35:17,995 --> 01:35:19,203
If God existed,

1546
01:35:20,412 --> 01:35:22,662
He wouldn't have
made us suffer like this.

1547
01:35:23,537 --> 01:35:25,662
He only tests the
patience of his devotees,

1548
01:35:26,495 --> 01:35:27,995
but he will not fail to help them.

1549
01:35:29,203 --> 01:35:32,078
He knows very well how to
save devotees who are in danger.

1550
01:35:32,662 --> 01:35:33,662
You stay calm and peaceful.

1551
01:35:34,203 --> 01:35:35,870
I will secure bail and bring
Venkata Ramana back.

1552
01:35:48,453 --> 01:35:51,578
Give me 50 lakhs
and I won't raid.

1553
01:35:52,328 --> 01:35:53,453
-It's mandatory.
-Sir!

1554
01:35:54,037 --> 01:35:55,453
One minute. He is on the phone.

1555
01:35:57,078 --> 01:35:57,745
What is it?

1556
01:35:57,912 --> 01:35:59,287
Sir, you raided my
house the other day...

1557
01:35:59,495 --> 01:36:01,703
and seized all the money,
books, and important documents.

1558
01:36:02,412 --> 01:36:05,873
Among them, there is an
important book called "God's Gift."

1559
01:36:05,953 --> 01:36:06,995
Please give me just that.

1560
01:36:07,912 --> 01:36:08,578
Listen, man.

1561
01:36:08,912 --> 01:36:12,828
There are many procedures, whether it
is the God's Gift book or any other book.

1562
01:36:13,120 --> 01:36:14,578
No, sir. Please, sir.
Please give me that.

1563
01:36:14,703 --> 01:36:17,203
-We will inform you. Go.
-Sir, that is very important to me.

1564
01:36:17,370 --> 01:36:18,953
-Hey, throw him out!
-Sir!

1565
01:36:19,287 --> 01:36:20,370
-Go.
-Come.

1566
01:36:20,703 --> 01:36:21,995
-Sir, just once.
-Go.

1567
01:36:27,453 --> 01:36:29,537
Mom, where's our car?

1568
01:36:30,245 --> 01:36:31,245
We should buy it, son.

1569
01:36:34,995 --> 01:36:36,870
-Mom, it's raining.
-It's raining, mom.

1570
01:36:37,495 --> 01:36:39,662
-Mom, let's go there.
-Let's go there.

1571
01:36:40,328 --> 01:36:41,120
Hurry up.

1572
01:36:42,328 --> 01:36:43,412
Come inside quickly.

1573
01:36:49,203 --> 01:36:50,620
Padma.
Padma.

1574
01:36:51,037 --> 01:36:53,328
Hey, she has gone to pick up the kids from
school.

1575
01:36:53,703 --> 01:36:54,662
-Is it?
-Yes.

1576
01:36:54,787 --> 01:36:55,703
It's raining out side.

1577
01:36:57,245 --> 01:36:58,912
-Okay, I will go and get them.
-Okay.

1578
01:37:22,453 --> 01:37:24,078
-Mom.
-Mom.

1579
01:37:24,370 --> 01:37:26,828
[screaming]

1580
01:37:27,745 --> 01:37:28,870
Mommy.

1581
01:37:39,870 --> 01:37:40,912
Padma.

1582
01:37:43,036 --> 01:37:44,603
Padma.

1583
01:37:48,536 --> 01:37:49,955
Balaji.

1584
01:38:13,412 --> 01:38:14,328
Doctor.

1585
01:38:14,870 --> 01:38:16,912
Your wife won't survive
more than 3 hours.

1586
01:38:17,245 --> 01:38:18,328
I am sorry, venkata Ramana.

1587
01:38:21,203 --> 01:38:22,037
Padma.

1588
01:38:23,703 --> 01:38:27,328
Lord Brahma writes the ultimate
retribution for every sin a human commits.

1589
01:38:27,578 --> 01:38:30,703
Karma will hunt you
down for altering that fate.

1590
01:38:30,953 --> 01:38:31,703
Karma will hunt you!

1591
01:38:31,953 --> 01:38:32,828
Padma.

1592
01:38:43,078 --> 01:38:44,453
Hey, who is inside?

1593
01:38:47,912 --> 01:38:48,912
Who are you all?

1594
01:38:49,203 --> 01:38:50,203
We are O.G. men.

1595
01:39:02,037 --> 01:39:05,703
-Yassu, sit here. I'll be back soon.
-Okay, mom.

1596
01:39:17,327 --> 01:39:20,333
[Cell phone rings]

1597
01:39:22,245 --> 01:39:24,037
Brother-in-law,
my car has started.

1598
01:39:24,287 --> 01:39:26,328
-Is it?
-Location has also been traced.

1599
01:39:26,495 --> 01:39:28,037
Then share the
location immediately.

1600
01:39:28,495 --> 01:39:32,328
My life is ruined because of what
Venkata Ramana has written in the book.

1601
01:39:32,495 --> 01:39:34,537
You come quickly.
Let's go and get the book.

1602
01:39:40,328 --> 01:39:43,870
I don't know if you will cross
the seven seas or the seven hills.

1603
01:39:44,828 --> 01:39:46,828
Please save my wife who
took seven steps with me.

1604
01:39:48,662 --> 01:39:49,662
Save her, Lord.

1605
01:39:50,787 --> 01:39:51,787
Venkata Ramana.

1606
01:39:52,495 --> 01:39:53,787
We know where the book is.

1607
01:39:55,078 --> 01:39:55,745
Auto.

1608
01:39:56,037 --> 01:39:56,828
-Sir!
-Hey, Bhaskar.

1609
01:39:57,078 --> 01:39:58,537
-We must go to a place immediately.
-Okay, sir. Get in.

1610
01:39:58,999 --> 01:39:59,787
Go quickly.

1611
01:40:01,412 --> 01:40:05,203
OG,
I have brought the one who stole your car.

1612
01:40:19,287 --> 01:40:20,620
Why did you kidnap me?

1613
01:40:20,745 --> 01:40:21,745
Who are you guys?

1614
01:40:21,828 --> 01:40:26,537
I am the only original
gangster in this Hyderabad city.

1615
01:40:27,037 --> 01:40:28,037
I am OG.

1616
01:40:28,162 --> 01:40:30,870
You look very lazy.
How can you be OG?

1617
01:40:30,995 --> 01:40:34,787
I'm the kingpin of this Hyderabad city.
How dare you steal my car?

1618
01:40:35,037 --> 01:40:39,620
Where is the Range Rover bearing
the number 9999 that you stole?

1619
01:40:39,703 --> 01:40:41,995
I sold it for 9 lakhs as it was all nines!

1620
01:40:42,162 --> 01:40:45,328
I paid 9 lakhs just to obtain
that registration number!

1621
01:40:45,453 --> 01:40:47,787
How can you sell the car for that price?

1622
01:40:47,995 --> 01:40:49,203
[OG groans]

1623
01:40:49,328 --> 01:40:51,828
Yuck!
Do you realize where you took it out from?

1624
01:40:51,953 --> 01:40:55,957
Will you pay me fifty million
for my car or should I shoot you?

1625
01:40:56,037 --> 01:40:58,245
I think they are going to kill Daddy!

1626
01:40:58,370 --> 01:40:59,578
Ouch! Ah!

1627
01:41:00,162 --> 01:41:01,578
Ah!

1628
01:41:22,912 --> 01:41:30,037
Fifty million rupees should appear in
the car bearing the number TG 28 DL 0255.

1629
01:41:30,203 --> 01:41:32,912
Om Namo Venkateshaya!

1630
01:41:53,037 --> 01:41:54,037
Uncle,

1631
01:41:54,203 --> 01:41:56,120
Your fifty million is in the car boot.

1632
01:41:56,203 --> 01:41:57,537
Don't harm my dad.

1633
01:41:57,787 --> 01:41:58,787
Eh?

1634
01:42:00,537 --> 01:42:01,620
Open it.

1635
01:42:07,745 --> 01:42:10,328
How dare you play with me
with the money in the boot?

1636
01:42:10,453 --> 01:42:13,537
My dad doesn't know how
the money came into the boot.

1637
01:42:14,203 --> 01:42:15,203
Do you know?

1638
01:42:15,370 --> 01:42:17,620
Yes, I do. They appeared
when I wrote it in this book.

1639
01:42:18,995 --> 01:42:21,328
You mean the money appeared
when you wrote it in this book?

1640
01:42:21,453 --> 01:42:24,245
Yes, uncle. Whatever we
write in this book will come true.

1641
01:42:24,412 --> 01:42:26,370
-Anything we write will come true?
-Yeah.

1642
01:42:26,870 --> 01:42:28,662
Give me that book.

1643
01:42:53,037 --> 01:42:56,037
OG, this looks like a precious book.

1644
01:42:56,453 --> 01:42:57,995
Think twice before you write anything.

1645
01:43:02,995 --> 01:43:10,912
A container full of money should come
to shed no.3 in the aluminum factory.

1646
01:43:16,537 --> 01:43:18,578
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1647
01:44:00,203 --> 01:44:01,787
Look what happens now.

1648
01:44:02,037 --> 01:44:05,828
I will buy all the lands in Amaravati
with this container full of money.

1649
01:44:06,537 --> 01:44:10,453
OG,
you need power to maintain such wealth.

1650
01:44:12,120 --> 01:44:13,578
[OG laughs]

1651
01:44:14,162 --> 01:44:20,745
I, Chapala Suresh, want to be the
permanent chief minister of this nation.

1652
01:44:21,412 --> 01:44:23,787
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1653
01:44:27,078 --> 01:44:29,078
Huh! Oh no! What is this?

1654
01:44:29,370 --> 01:44:30,495
Book on fire!

1655
01:44:31,745 --> 01:44:34,162
If you write something wrong in the book,
the page will burn.

1656
01:44:34,245 --> 01:44:35,495
That's in the rules of the book.

1657
01:44:35,662 --> 01:44:37,537
-I wrote it right.
-What did you write, OG?

1658
01:44:38,287 --> 01:44:41,453
I wrote that I want to be the
permanent chief minister of this nation.

1659
01:44:44,745 --> 01:44:46,870
He looks like a complete fool

1660
01:44:47,953 --> 01:44:50,457
You should have specified 'for the world',
the book would have been turned to ashes!

1661
01:44:50,537 --> 01:44:52,078
There's no chief minister for a nation,
OG.

1662
01:44:52,162 --> 01:44:53,162
It's for a state!

1663
01:44:53,328 --> 01:44:54,578
Oh!

1664
01:44:54,662 --> 01:44:56,995
OG, I beg you.

1665
01:44:57,412 --> 01:44:58,662
This is a precious book.

1666
01:44:58,787 --> 01:45:01,203
Think twice and write correctly.

1667
01:45:02,828 --> 01:45:03,828
The last page.

1668
01:45:05,287 --> 01:45:06,287
I will write correctly.

1669
01:45:06,370 --> 01:45:07,370
Hello, OG.

1670
01:45:07,828 --> 01:45:09,328
I found that book in my car.

1671
01:45:09,412 --> 01:45:10,995
Give me the last page to write.

1672
01:45:11,078 --> 01:45:12,040
I won't give it to anyone.

1673
01:45:12,120 --> 01:45:13,120
I will write it myself.

1674
01:45:13,245 --> 01:45:15,412
Is it a festival receipt book?

1675
01:45:15,495 --> 01:45:18,203
-Any random person would write in it?
-Who are you clad in a towel?

1676
01:45:18,662 --> 01:45:22,078
An important part is missing in my body,
brother.

1677
01:45:22,578 --> 01:45:26,162
If I want it to come back,
I need this page.

1678
01:45:26,328 --> 01:45:28,537
-Please give me this page.
-What did you say?

1679
01:45:29,037 --> 01:45:31,328
-It's that one.
-What do you mean 'that one'?

1680
01:45:31,870 --> 01:45:33,245
How do I say?

1681
01:45:35,828 --> 01:45:38,415
A very important part, brother.

1682
01:45:38,495 --> 01:45:40,662
A very important part, brother!

1683
01:45:40,787 --> 01:45:42,953
-What's that?
-I'm unable to tell you.

1684
01:45:43,037 --> 01:45:44,037
Then show me.

1685
01:45:44,245 --> 01:45:47,162
Wait, I will show you.

1686
01:45:47,370 --> 01:45:48,165
Move.

1687
01:45:48,245 --> 01:45:49,620
Here it is.

1688
01:45:49,745 --> 01:45:51,037
Hey! Damn you!

1689
01:45:51,120 --> 01:45:53,037
Do you think you have
some ramp walk thighs?

1690
01:45:53,120 --> 01:45:54,662
Show me that important part.

1691
01:45:55,370 --> 01:45:56,370
See.

1692
01:46:01,453 --> 01:46:02,287
How did you miss such an important part?

1693
01:46:02,412 --> 01:46:04,037
I wrote it in that book
and it disappeared.

1694
01:46:04,120 --> 01:46:05,537
I'll get it back if I write it again.

1695
01:46:05,662 --> 01:46:06,787
Move aside.

1696
01:46:06,870 --> 01:46:09,537
Sir. He has a matter problem
and I have a money problem.

1697
01:46:09,787 --> 01:46:11,703
I sold my properties and
ended up on the streets.

1698
01:46:12,120 --> 01:46:14,078
Please give me that book.
I will write in it.

1699
01:46:14,203 --> 01:46:15,662
I won't give it. I will write in it.

1700
01:46:15,870 --> 01:46:16,870
Sir, my book.

1701
01:46:16,953 --> 01:46:17,995
Hey! Who are you?

1702
01:46:18,078 --> 01:46:20,078
-He's the actual owner of this book, sir.
-Yes, sir.

1703
01:46:20,162 --> 01:46:22,870
How many owners does this book have?

1704
01:46:23,149 --> 01:46:24,662
My wife is on the death bed, sir.

1705
01:46:26,274 --> 01:46:28,578
-I need this page to save my wife.
-I won't give it.

1706
01:46:28,828 --> 01:46:29,828
I will write in it.

1707
01:46:30,662 --> 01:46:31,662
You have to give it.

1708
01:46:31,912 --> 01:46:33,245
Hey! Who is it now?

1709
01:46:33,412 --> 01:46:35,245
If he is Rama, I'm Hanuman.

1710
01:46:35,328 --> 01:46:37,370
If he is Krishna, I'm Kuchela.

1711
01:46:37,453 --> 01:46:39,953
If he is a political star,
I'm a power star.

1712
01:46:40,662 --> 01:46:44,620
He is a God who gave me a crore to
drop him at Manikonda from Kukatpally.

1713
01:46:44,995 --> 01:46:46,457
I don't know if God exists or not.

1714
01:46:46,537 --> 01:46:47,787
Bhaskar, God exists.

1715
01:46:47,870 --> 01:46:49,453
-I saw him.
-You saw him, sir.

1716
01:46:49,745 --> 01:46:51,078
But these scoundrels didn't.

1717
01:46:51,162 --> 01:46:52,662
Whom are you calling a scoundrel?

1718
01:46:53,328 --> 01:46:54,828
Oh damn!

1719
01:46:55,162 --> 01:46:56,203
[groans]

1720
01:47:04,245 --> 01:47:06,370
Hey, thrash him.

1721
01:47:06,787 --> 01:47:09,370
Sir, he is innocent. Don't harm him.

1722
01:47:09,578 --> 01:47:11,203
Hey, kill him.

1723
01:47:11,495 --> 01:47:12,537
Sir, sir, sir.

1724
01:47:19,287 --> 01:47:20,328
Does he look innocent?

1725
01:47:28,328 --> 01:47:30,412
Where did they go?
Did they run away?

1726
01:47:30,787 --> 01:47:32,203
You turned the other side, man!

1727
01:47:34,203 --> 01:47:36,495
I won't leave anyone even
if they're hiding behind me.

1728
01:47:45,953 --> 01:47:49,037
Why did you bend down when the trident
is rotating above you? Bloody fools!

1729
01:47:49,120 --> 01:47:51,207
We know that the trident
will hit us if we get up!

1730
01:47:51,287 --> 01:47:52,370
I too shall bend down then!

1731
01:47:59,037 --> 01:48:00,578
Sir, sir, sir. Ask them to stop.

1732
01:48:00,703 --> 01:48:03,203
You ask him not to rotate the trident.
He thinks it's some toy.

1733
01:48:10,120 --> 01:48:11,120
Akhanda.

1734
01:48:11,495 --> 01:48:13,287
No, Akhanda 2.

1735
01:48:13,787 --> 01:48:16,662
If you give it, you will lose the book.
or else, you will lose your life.

1736
01:48:17,537 --> 01:48:19,370
Decide it, you bloody fools.

1737
01:48:19,703 --> 01:48:20,703
Phuket.

1738
01:48:20,870 --> 01:48:21,870
Bangkok.

1739
01:48:23,870 --> 01:48:25,203
-Hey!
-Hey!

1740
01:48:25,662 --> 01:48:27,370
Keep your voice low.

1741
01:48:27,870 --> 01:48:31,537
I don't know which voice I will laugh
at and which voice I shall cut the throat.

1742
01:48:31,953 --> 01:48:33,870
I can't even imagine it, you scoundrel.

1743
01:48:46,370 --> 01:48:47,578
Huh?

1744
01:48:47,953 --> 01:48:49,120
And he says he is an O.G.

1745
01:48:49,453 --> 01:48:50,828
You're just a cabbage.

1746
01:48:51,328 --> 01:48:52,537
Save your wife, sir.

1747
01:48:59,203 --> 01:49:00,165
Book.

1748
01:49:00,245 --> 01:49:02,537
-Hey!
-Leave me.

1749
01:49:02,662 --> 01:49:03,912
It's mine.

1750
01:49:04,037 --> 01:49:05,037
Leave me.

1751
01:49:07,203 --> 01:49:08,203
Lord!

1752
01:49:08,537 --> 01:49:13,912
[echoes]

1753
01:49:14,296 --> 01:49:15,328
Tell me, Venkataramana.

1754
01:49:15,453 --> 01:49:16,953
Please save me for this time, Lord.

1755
01:49:19,162 --> 01:49:21,832
Who are you talking to,
like this is a reality show?

1756
01:49:21,912 --> 01:49:22,912
Who is there?

1757
01:49:23,078 --> 01:49:24,207
-The Lord.
-Which lord?

1758
01:49:24,287 --> 01:49:25,537
Is it Lord Hanuman or Ayyappa?

1759
01:49:25,662 --> 01:49:27,662
-It's Lord Venkateshwara.
-Oh! The Big Boss!

1760
01:49:29,060 --> 01:49:30,745
Lord... Please save me somehow.

1761
01:49:30,870 --> 01:49:32,495
Please save my wife, Swami.

1762
01:49:37,828 --> 01:49:38,995
Venkataramana.

1763
01:49:39,412 --> 01:49:42,245
If everything is done by God,
what is the reason a human exists?

1764
01:49:43,366 --> 01:49:47,412
A person who can't face a
problem can't achieve victory.

1765
01:49:48,602 --> 01:49:51,078
'Courage is the best tool.'

1766
01:49:51,370 --> 01:49:53,995
'Hardwork is the only way to success.'

1767
01:49:54,828 --> 01:49:58,162
'What can you achieve
in this world with fear?'

1768
01:49:58,912 --> 01:50:01,537
'No one can defeat a courageous person.'

1769
01:50:01,662 --> 01:50:03,703
[echoes]

1770
01:50:04,311 --> 01:50:05,703
What did Lord Venkateshwara say?

1771
01:50:05,912 --> 01:50:07,162
He asked me to face the problem.

1772
01:50:11,412 --> 01:50:12,412
Eh! Where is he?

1773
01:50:12,495 --> 01:50:13,828
There! He is running!

1774
01:50:22,745 --> 01:50:24,537
Venkataramana...
Venkataramana... Venkataramana.

1775
01:50:24,662 --> 01:50:25,623
Listen to me.

1776
01:50:25,703 --> 01:50:26,578
Oh my!

1777
01:50:26,953 --> 01:50:28,537
Venkataramana I beg you.

1778
01:50:28,620 --> 01:50:30,078
Give me the book.
I will give you a good gift.

1779
01:50:30,203 --> 01:50:31,953
He hit me!

1780
01:50:39,245 --> 01:50:40,207
Stop it!

1781
01:50:40,287 --> 01:50:42,328
Looks like you're going to
kill me before the book comes.

1782
01:50:42,412 --> 01:50:43,912
All of you hit him.

1783
01:50:48,537 --> 01:50:49,537
Hey.

1784
01:50:49,620 --> 01:50:50,620
Oh my!

1785
01:51:04,370 --> 01:51:05,412
Move aside!

1786
01:51:10,120 --> 01:51:11,745
Hey! Let go!

1787
01:51:12,662 --> 01:51:13,745
Let go of me.

1788
01:51:16,953 --> 01:51:17,953
Lord!

1789
01:51:20,748 --> 01:51:26,537
[God] 'The book should not touch the
ground under any circumstances.'

1790
01:51:27,037 --> 01:51:30,995
'If that happens,
the book will lose its power.'

1791
01:51:35,078 --> 01:51:37,078
Huh?

1792
01:51:37,745 --> 01:51:39,495
Ah! Damn!

1793
01:51:42,370 --> 01:51:43,370
Where are you?

1794
01:51:43,873 --> 01:51:45,578
[OG panting]

1795
01:52:01,453 --> 01:52:02,078
As it--

1796
01:52:02,370 --> 01:52:03,162
Ah!

1797
01:52:11,453 --> 01:52:12,870
As it is.

1798
01:52:13,662 --> 01:52:16,787
[echoes]

1799
01:52:16,870 --> 01:52:19,120
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1800
01:52:19,453 --> 01:52:23,573
[echoes]

1801
01:52:23,653 --> 01:52:28,324
[Sanskrit]

1802
01:53:10,953 --> 01:53:11,995
Huh!

1803
01:53:12,912 --> 01:53:15,037
OG! O...

1804
01:53:17,453 --> 01:53:18,620
OG, look there.

1805
01:53:20,203 --> 01:53:21,537
Hey! Hey! Hey!

1806
01:53:22,370 --> 01:53:24,078
Hey! Hey! Lord!

1807
01:53:24,158 --> 01:53:25,870
[echoes]

1808
01:53:26,120 --> 01:53:27,870
Huh? Lord!

1809
01:53:27,953 --> 01:53:29,620
[echoes]

1810
01:53:29,828 --> 01:53:30,828
What is this?

1811
01:53:30,912 --> 01:53:33,495
The Lord answers him,
but my words just echo back.

1812
01:53:33,840 --> 01:53:35,995
Brother, you have gone mad.

1813
01:53:37,793 --> 01:53:41,123
Brother-in-law. I think I got mine back.

1814
01:53:41,203 --> 01:53:44,953
If you got yours, I would also
have got all my property back.

1815
01:53:45,287 --> 01:53:46,287
Lord!

1816
01:53:46,796 --> 01:53:49,953
We will never wish
for others' destruction.

1817
01:53:56,340 --> 01:53:58,120
-Brother.
-Brother-in-law.

1818
01:53:58,553 --> 01:53:59,453
I know it, dear.

1819
01:53:59,836 --> 01:54:02,495
Doctors said that your
sister-in-law will not live.

1820
01:54:02,911 --> 01:54:04,703
Who is dying? Sister-in-law is alive.

1821
01:54:04,828 --> 01:54:05,828
She is alive?

1822
01:54:05,953 --> 01:54:06,995
Why are you so shocked?

1823
01:54:07,078 --> 01:54:09,162
-Don't you want her to live?
-Shut up.

1824
01:54:09,412 --> 01:54:10,412
Venkataramana.

1825
01:54:10,495 --> 01:54:13,495
One Dr. Venkateswara Rao from T.T.D.
temple was here.

1826
01:54:13,662 --> 01:54:16,037
You gave 30 lakhs for
your children's operation.

1827
01:54:16,245 --> 01:54:18,412
Also, he himself operated on your wife.

1828
01:54:19,227 --> 01:54:20,203
Now she is safe.

1829
01:54:20,787 --> 01:54:22,745
If you want, you can meet him in CC Food.

1830
01:54:23,287 --> 01:54:24,287
Let's go.

1831
01:54:27,412 --> 01:54:28,412
Take a look, sir.

1832
01:54:28,495 --> 01:54:29,328
It's him.

1833
01:54:29,453 --> 01:54:31,953
I am Dr. Venkateshwara from Tirupati.

1834
01:54:32,078 --> 01:54:34,245
I came to operate on Padmavathi.

1835
01:54:34,370 --> 01:54:37,412
Sir, she will not live even if the
God himself performs this operation.

1836
01:54:37,995 --> 01:54:39,453
We will try sir.

1837
01:54:41,162 --> 01:54:47,828
The Tirumala Tirupati Devasthanam is
paying 30 lakhs for children's operation.

1838
01:55:00,203 --> 01:55:02,245
-[God] 'Venkataramana...'
-Lord!

1839
01:55:02,370 --> 01:55:07,412
'I took a loan of 30 lakhs from Kubera
for 5 percent interest to pay for this.'

1840
01:55:07,791 --> 01:55:10,537
'Return back this amount along
with the interest into my hundi.'

1841
01:55:10,620 --> 01:55:11,620
I shall, Lord.

1842
01:55:12,037 --> 01:55:13,328
I will put it in the hundi.

1843
01:55:18,271 --> 01:55:19,474
-Priest.
-What is it?

1844
01:55:19,554 --> 01:55:20,787
We will look for a house
in 2 days and leave.

1845
01:55:20,870 --> 01:55:21,870
-Why?
-But why?

1846
01:55:22,310 --> 01:55:25,207
We're having Chakkerapongali,
Daddhojanam and Pulihora happily.

1847
01:55:25,287 --> 01:55:26,162
Why leave?

1848
01:55:26,287 --> 01:55:27,287
Come on, Father.

1849
01:55:28,995 --> 01:55:30,037
Daddy.

1850
01:55:30,662 --> 01:55:32,078
I have to tell you something.

1851
01:55:32,267 --> 01:55:34,620
What is it? You have been
trying to say something for 2 days.

1852
01:55:34,703 --> 01:55:35,703
What is it?

1853
01:55:42,396 --> 01:55:45,162
I tore a page out of your book.

1854
01:55:50,353 --> 01:55:51,245
Lord of the seven hills!

1855
01:55:54,342 --> 01:55:55,495
Take the pen, Venkataramana.

1856
01:55:55,974 --> 01:55:56,828
Write carefully.

1857
01:55:57,245 --> 01:56:00,203
Think well and write so that
we get the money this time.

1858
01:56:00,404 --> 01:56:01,446
Write it without fear.

1859
01:56:01,821 --> 01:56:04,446
Write that all the jewelry from a
prestigious shop should come to our house.

1860
01:56:04,571 --> 01:56:05,571
Write.

1861
01:56:08,114 --> 01:56:13,738
Whatever my wife
Padmavathi threw in the lake...

1862
01:56:14,863 --> 01:56:18,529
those Lord's jewelry should be found.

1863
01:56:20,796 --> 01:56:23,571
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1864
01:56:50,729 --> 01:56:51,529
Thank God!

1865
01:56:51,696 --> 01:56:52,988
We found the jewellery sack.

1866
01:56:54,815 --> 01:56:57,779
Venkataramana, Shall we sell the
jewellery and settle down in Dubai?

1867
01:56:57,988 --> 01:56:59,988
Can we find Lord
Venkateshwara in Dubai too?

1868
01:57:00,154 --> 01:57:02,013
Lord is all over the world.

1869
01:57:15,993 --> 01:57:16,779
Govinda.

1870
01:57:17,409 --> 01:57:21,571
The truth that a human
has to go up stage by stage...

1871
01:57:22,727 --> 01:57:25,446
Didn't register well in
this middle class mind.

1872
01:57:25,744 --> 01:57:27,654
I wanted to get to the top at a time.

1873
01:57:28,122 --> 01:57:29,488
But I failed, my Lord!

1874
01:57:30,654 --> 01:57:34,571
I wanted to earn crores without
even 100 rupees in my pocket.

1875
01:57:35,862 --> 01:57:37,613
We have to work hard to earn money.

1876
01:57:38,446 --> 01:57:42,446
If we take shortcuts, we would be doomed.

1877
01:57:44,196 --> 01:57:46,446
I foolishly asked for your jewellery.

1878
01:57:47,095 --> 01:57:48,113
Forgive me, Lord.

1879
01:57:49,613 --> 01:57:51,738
Venkataramana... Forgive me.

1880
01:57:52,154 --> 01:57:55,029
I was greedy for the golden
bracelet and made a mistake.

1881
01:57:55,463 --> 01:57:57,321
My business is ruined.

1882
01:57:57,404 --> 01:57:59,863
I lost my shop in road extension.

1883
01:58:00,029 --> 01:58:02,363
The Lord's gold bracelet is all yours.

1884
01:58:11,821 --> 01:58:13,613
I gave all your jewellery to you.

1885
01:58:14,069 --> 01:58:19,529
I forgot that God knows when and
where to give something to a person.

1886
01:58:21,183 --> 01:58:22,738
I don't need anything else, Lord.

1887
01:58:23,654 --> 01:58:24,863
I just need your blessings.

1888
01:58:25,363 --> 01:58:27,113
Om Namo Venkateshaya.

1889
01:58:34,503 --> 01:58:37,779
[snoring]

1890
01:58:39,321 --> 01:58:41,321
[groaning] Huh!

1891
01:58:42,363 --> 01:58:43,613
Is it a lightning bolt?

1892
01:58:45,872 --> 01:58:46,904
Hey!

1893
01:58:53,071 --> 01:58:54,071
Sir.

1894
01:58:54,363 --> 01:58:55,821
-The book...
-Hey Bhaskar!

1895
01:58:56,113 --> 01:58:58,946
Sir... Is this a wallet to keep losing it?

1896
01:58:59,196 --> 01:59:00,821
It's a book. Careful, sir.

1897
01:59:01,779 --> 01:59:02,779
Lord!

1898
01:59:03,696 --> 01:59:05,113
Why are you looking up, sir?

1899
01:59:07,821 --> 01:59:08,863
Oh!

1900
01:59:11,906 --> 01:59:13,363
Who is up there?

1901
01:59:16,933 --> 01:59:21,571
OM NAMO VENKATESHAYA

